14:51.054 --> 14:54.263
- ♪ <i>Get around, I get around</i> ♪
- ♪ <i>Round, round, I get around</i> ♪

14:54.429 --> 14:57.388
-♪ <i>Get around, round, round
I get around</i> ♪ -[vocalizing]

14:57.554 --> 15:00.596
♪ <i>Get around, round, round
I get around</i> ♪

15:00.763 --> 15:03.804
♪ <i>Get around, round, round
I get around</i> ♪

15:03.971 --> 15:06.013
♪ <i>Get around, round, round
I get around...</i> ♪

15:06.179 --> 15:08.679
- [ominous music]
- [door rumbling]

15:08.846 --> 15:10.346
[clanking]

15:18.304 --> 15:19.388
[alarm blares]

15:19.554 --> 15:21.471
[dramatic music]

15:21.638 --> 15:23.679
[squelching]

15:27.888 --> 15:30.179
[clinking and buzzing]

15:30.346 --> 15:31.596
[engine rumbling]

15:32.846 --> 15:34.054
[alarm blaring]

15:38.929 --> 15:40.971
[music increases]

15:46.596 --> 15:47.679
[buzz and click]

15:48.679 --> 15:50.197
-[gentle music playing] -[woman
on tape] <i>Making the decision</i>

15:50.221 --> 15:51.638
<i>to change your life</i>

15:52.263 --> 15:55.304
<i>- is a courageous first step.</i>
- [engine rumbling]

15:55.471 --> 15:58.471
<i>Once you're convinced
of the need for change,</i>

15:58.929 --> 16:02.554
some of <i>that courage will need
to be directed outward</i>

16:03.304 --> 16:07.013
<i>into a world that would prefer
you stay exactly as you are.</i>

16:08.763 --> 16:12.179
<i>Dealing with difficult
and confrontational people</i>

16:12.346 --> 16:14.971
<i>is, like many things, a skill</i>

16:15.596 --> 16:17.263
<i>that can be developed over time,</i>

16:17.763 --> 16:21.929
<i>-but no change is
possible without...</i> -[sighs]

16:25.888 --> 16:27.721
[Griffin]
Well, shithead?

16:29.346 --> 16:30.513
I told you, Griffin,

16:31.304 --> 16:34.638
can't help you. I wish I could,
but I can't. Sorry.

16:34.804 --> 16:37.388
I knew you were stupid, I
didn't think you were that stupid.

16:37.554 --> 16:39.554
Uh, I'm not stupid. [chuckle]

16:40.179 --> 16:43.459
I mean, I... listen, I get you're my boss
and all, and I would help you if I could,

16:43.554 --> 16:45.388
- but it's messed up for me...
- [beep]

16:45.554 --> 16:48.221
vis-ä-vis my, you know,
personal situation,

16:48.388 --> 16:50.179
and I'm not gonna do it.

16:50.638 --> 16:51.971
Okay, so you'll think about it.

16:52.429 --> 16:53.971
No. I wish I didn't
even know about it.

16:54.138 --> 16:56.138
What's the big goddamn deal?
Nobody's gonna know!

16:56.304 --> 16:57.513
[Teacake scoffs]

16:58.971 --> 17:00.388
I've heard those words before.

17:02.138 --> 17:04.429
- You do it.
- [Griffin] I don't work nights,

17:04.596 --> 17:06.864
- and no one's gonna come for that shit in the daytime.
- Well...

17:06.888 --> 17:09.596
So, just let 'em in so you
and me don't have a problem.

17:09.763 --> 17:11.003
Why do we gotta have a problem?

17:11.138 --> 17:12.138
'Cause you know,

17:12.721 --> 17:13.971
but you're not in,

17:14.138 --> 17:16.804
and if you're not in
and you know,

17:17.304 --> 17:18.638
then we got a problem.

17:23.138 --> 17:24.721
You got the new help tonight.

17:24.888 --> 17:27.013
She's on walk and lock check
till 12:00.

17:27.929 --> 17:29.888
- [Teacake]What's her name?
- [crickets chirping]

17:30.054 --> 17:31.304
Don't get any ideas.

17:31.763 --> 17:33.388
She's already hitting on me.

17:34.304 --> 17:35.679
Ugh. [scoffs]

17:35.846 --> 17:37.763
[engine starts]

17:37.929 --> 17:40.179
[Griffin] Something's
beeping in there! Fix it!

17:40.346 --> 17:42.306
- [clattering]
- [Teacake] Wait, what? [scoffs]

17:43.846 --> 17:44.846
Asshole.

17:45.888 --> 17:47.679
- [deeply sighs]
- [clattering]

17:55.471 --> 17:57.513
[suspenseful music]

17:59.346 --> 18:02.013
- [clacking]
- [footsteps approaching]

18:18.638 --> 18:20.763
[buzzing]

18:20.929 --> 18:23.447
-[engines rumbling] -[man on
radio] <i>...expect heavy rain tonight,</i>

18:23.471 --> 18:26.513
<i>with showers starting in the early
evening and intensifying overnight.</i>

18:26.679 --> 18:29.929
<i>Thunderstorms are likely with strong
gusts of wind and potential local...</i>

18:30.096 --> 18:31.138
[engine shuts off]

18:32.138 --> 18:34.846
[deeply breathes]

18:35.013 --> 18:36.929
[doorbell jingles]

18:38.179 --> 18:41.179
Ah, Mrs. Rooney,
how's it going? Staying cool?

18:41.346 --> 18:45.013
[Rooney]
I need to get into SB-114.

18:45.179 --> 18:46.804
It's my anniversary.

18:47.304 --> 18:49.471
Ah, okay. Superhot out, right?

18:49.638 --> 18:51.846
Kinda weird this time of year,
but I guess we gotta...

18:52.013 --> 18:53.846
I need to get into it quick.

18:54.471 --> 18:57.679
God, absolutely. Storage
emergency... [chuckles] I totally get it.

18:57.846 --> 19:00.763
-[rumbling] -It's snowing,
it's sunny, it's raining, it's hot,

19:00.929 --> 19:03.409
I... I don't know, but guess we
gotta get used to it, you know?

19:03.471 --> 19:05.513
-Global warming... -[Rooney]
Could you stop talking?

19:05.971 --> 19:08.596
Yeah. Please,
let me get the elevator for you.

19:08.763 --> 19:09.804
Just one sec.

19:11.013 --> 19:12.221
[beep]

19:12.388 --> 19:14.346
All right there,
Mrs. Rooney. Uh, well,

19:14.513 --> 19:16.833
try not to get lost down there.
It can be pretty confusing,

19:16.929 --> 19:18.804
I mean, even for me,
and I'm here every day.

19:18.971 --> 19:20.780
- [elevator voice] <i>Going down.</i>
- [Teacake] Keep an eye on you!

19:20.804 --> 19:22.888
[Rooney]
Fifty-two years...

19:23.346 --> 19:25.388
[elevator whirring]

19:26.346 --> 19:28.096
- [softly chuckles]
- [soft ding]

19:35.179 --> 19:36.179
Hmm.

19:36.346 --> 19:37.679
- [ding]
<i>- Sub-level one.</i>

19:38.638 --> 19:41.263
- [suspenseful music]
- [deeply exhales]

19:43.346 --> 19:45.638
[clicking and buzzing]

19:45.804 --> 19:47.846
[heavily breathing]

19:52.929 --> 19:54.971
- [rattling]
- [grunting]

20:00.346 --> 20:01.971
- [click]
- [grunts]

20:07.596 --> 20:09.846
[rattling]

20:12.013 --> 20:13.429
[clacking]

20:14.679 --> 20:15.929
[muttering]

20:17.971 --> 20:20.221
- [grunts]
- [gentle music]

20:22.429 --> 20:24.263
[softly] Happy anniversary.

20:24.429 --> 20:26.388
[soft chuckling]

20:32.638 --> 20:33.638
Okay.

20:37.096 --> 20:39.138
[ominous music]

20:40.971 --> 20:41.971
[sighs]

20:47.929 --> 20:49.054
Maybe...

20:53.304 --> 20:54.638
maybe first...

20:55.888 --> 20:56.929
we'll have a nap.

20:59.096 --> 21:00.929
[grunts]

21:05.013 --> 21:07.138
[woman on tape]
<i>Feeling unhappy, stressed,</i>

21:07.304 --> 21:09.264
<i>- and exhausted as a result...</i>
- [deeply breathes]

21:09.346 --> 21:11.026
<i>- of constantly putting...</i>
- [soft sing]

21:11.138 --> 21:13.763
<i>other people's priorities
ahead of yours...</i>

21:24.804 --> 21:25.804
[ding]

21:26.388 --> 21:27.221
Huh...

21:27.346 --> 21:29.388
[suspenseful music]

21:40.554 --> 21:41.763
[mic feedback]

21:42.638 --> 21:44.804
S... sorry. Hello.

21:44.971 --> 21:47.888
Uh, c... can I get your opinion
on something? Real quick?

21:48.054 --> 21:49.721
- [feedback]
- [clears throat]

21:49.888 --> 21:50.888
Sorry again.

21:53.596 --> 21:55.316
So, what? You just started
picking up shifts

21:55.388 --> 21:56.846
- this week or...
- [shushes]

21:58.846 --> 21:59.846
Sorry.

22:01.013 --> 22:02.263
[deeply exhales]

22:02.846 --> 22:04.554
Yeah, it's a pretty shit job,
you know...

22:04.721 --> 22:06.554
- [grunts]
- But whatever.

22:07.846 --> 22:09.471
Discount on storage. [chuckles]

22:10.804 --> 22:13.846
I got a lot of thoughts on that
though. Basically, don't do it.

22:14.013 --> 22:16.221
Hanging onto all your shit
forever? [clicks tongue]

22:16.388 --> 22:18.221
It's a really terrible idea.

22:19.554 --> 22:22.263
This whole industry is a racket.
It's like crack.

22:22.846 --> 22:24.971
You just keep piling more
and more shit in there,

22:25.138 --> 22:27.018
and pretty soon,
you can't throw anything out...

22:27.054 --> 22:28.054
I don't hear anything.

22:28.513 --> 22:29.679
Well, I definitely heard it.

22:30.263 --> 22:32.096
Well, not definitely.
I mean, I was, like,

22:32.263 --> 22:34.221
I don't know, aware of it,
you know what I mean?

22:34.388 --> 22:36.508
Like, I was having an argument
with my brain about it.

22:37.346 --> 22:38.763
Does, does that
ever happen to you?

22:39.971 --> 22:41.763
You are very chatty.

22:41.929 --> 22:43.221
[chuckling] Uh, yeah, I know.

22:43.763 --> 22:45.513
- It can be a problem.
- Mm.

22:47.929 --> 22:51.179
- I'm Teacake.
- Mm! "Teacake."

22:51.929 --> 22:53.179
You must have loved that book.

22:54.388 --> 22:58.054
- What book?
- You're named after a famous character from a book.

22:58.221 --> 23:00.929
Oh. [chuckles]
No, that ain't it.

23:02.304 --> 23:04.679
Long story.
Fairly annoying. [laughs]

23:04.846 --> 23:07.096
- [cell phone ringing]
- Oh.

23:07.263 --> 23:08.388
[clears throat]

23:10.304 --> 23:11.554
[sighs]

23:13.388 --> 23:15.638
- What?
- [man indistinctly speaking]

23:16.429 --> 23:20.054
- I said I do not want to hear it.
<i>- Listen, I've got a problem</i>...

23:20.221 --> 23:22.013
Yeah, well,
you always have a problem.

23:22.846 --> 23:24.326
- I've gotta go.
<i>- Don't hang up on</i>...

23:27.888 --> 23:31.429
[sighs] Long story.
Fairly annoying.

23:32.013 --> 23:33.721
- Yeah.
- [gentle music]

23:33.888 --> 23:35.638
- I'm Naomi.
- [clears throat]

23:37.554 --> 23:38.679
Nice to meet you.

23:42.638 --> 23:43.638
[ding]

23:44.096 --> 23:45.429
[chuckles]

23:45.596 --> 23:47.388
- See what I'm saying?
- [chuckling] Yeah.

23:47.554 --> 23:49.471
[light suspenseful music]

23:49.638 --> 23:51.554
- [crickets chirping]
- [Robert grunting]

23:51.721 --> 23:53.096
[cell phone buzzing]

23:53.596 --> 23:56.429
[mumbles and heavily breathes]

23:59.179 --> 24:00.263
[grunts]

24:01.179 --> 24:02.179
[click]

24:02.554 --> 24:03.846
[grunts]

24:07.429 --> 24:10.388
[mumbles] Hello?
[clears throat] Hello?

24:10.929 --> 24:13.721
[Abigail] <i>I'm calling about the
1978 Plymouth Duster for sale.</i>

24:17.721 --> 24:21.054
<i>- Are you there?</i>
- Give me five minutes. [grunts]

24:22.929 --> 24:25.013
[sighing]

24:25.179 --> 24:27.846
- Who was that?
- My other wife.

24:28.554 --> 24:30.739
How can you be funny right away
in the middle of the night?

24:30.763 --> 24:31.846
It's a gift.

24:32.971 --> 24:36.096
- One of the kids?
- No, new voice.

24:36.263 --> 24:37.513
I'm sure it's nothing.

24:37.679 --> 24:39.679
Somebody having a panic attack.

24:40.888 --> 24:42.846
- Go back to sleep.
- [grunts]

24:44.471 --> 24:46.679
[Robert groaning]

24:48.263 --> 24:50.304
[ominous tone]

24:52.721 --> 24:54.138
You wanna call Griffin?

24:54.304 --> 24:56.638
Under no circumstance
do I wanna call Griffin.

24:59.054 --> 25:00.554
He tried that shit
on you already?

25:01.513 --> 25:03.138
He's a pig. Pigs do.

25:03.304 --> 25:05.513
Damn, call the office.
Get his ass fired.

25:05.679 --> 25:08.471
Mm, it won't play out that way,
and I need the job.

25:08.638 --> 25:10.721
Did he ask you to flip those TVs
he racked yet?

25:12.096 --> 25:13.429
That has not come up.

25:13.596 --> 25:15.138
Oh, it will. Trust me.

25:15.804 --> 25:18.447
He's got, like, a million of 'em
stashed in a couple units, up there,

25:18.471 --> 25:19.679
- downstairs.
- [ding]

25:20.804 --> 25:22.221
- [chuckling]
- That.

25:24.971 --> 25:27.179
- [grunts]
- [whimsical music]

25:27.346 --> 25:29.554
- [ding]
- [gasping]

25:30.179 --> 25:31.888
- It's coming from inside the wall.
- Yeah.

25:35.804 --> 25:37.596
- Huh.
- [ding]

25:37.763 --> 25:39.013
[frustrated exhale]

25:39.179 --> 25:40.638
What do you wanna do about it?

25:40.804 --> 25:43.846
What I wanna do
is take this picture down,

25:44.013 --> 25:46.054
go to the tool closet,
grab a claw bar,

25:46.221 --> 25:48.304
smash a hole through
this cheap-ass gypsum Sheetrock,

25:48.471 --> 25:49.780
and see what the hell
is beeping back there.

25:49.804 --> 25:51.114
Well, I'm okay with that
if you are.

25:51.138 --> 25:52.498
W... I said that's
what I wanna do,

25:52.596 --> 25:54.072
- not what I'm gonna do.
- Oh, come on,

25:54.096 --> 25:56.054
we can, uh... we can hang
the picture back up

25:56.221 --> 25:59.096
over the hole to cover it, bring
in a piece of Sheetrock tomorrow.

25:59.263 --> 26:02.114
U... I'm pretty handy, I can help you
patch it up, nobody'll know the difference.

26:02.138 --> 26:04.971
- Why would we do that?
- I have a very curious nature.

26:05.138 --> 26:07.929
- Clearly. No, I don't think so.
- [cell phone ringing]

26:10.263 --> 26:12.054
- [click]
- It's my, uh...

26:13.221 --> 26:14.388
kid's dad.

26:15.263 --> 26:16.929
- Oh.
- High school.

26:17.471 --> 26:18.554
Shit happens.

26:19.138 --> 26:21.054
Yeah. That it does.

26:22.388 --> 26:24.638
He is a hopeless man-child,

26:24.804 --> 26:28.346
and that sort of shit makes
me wanna smash through walls.

26:28.513 --> 26:31.179
- Let's, let's do it.
- So we can see a dead smoke alarm?

26:31.346 --> 26:34.638
- I don't think so.
- Maybe it's a smoke alarm,

26:35.429 --> 26:38.054
but maybe
it's something terrible.

26:38.721 --> 26:41.221
I mean, we're guards, right?
We're supposed to guard the place.

26:41.388 --> 26:43.971
Yeah. You know,
I need this job too. [chuckles]

26:44.138 --> 26:45.738
[clicks tongue]
You're not gonna lose it.

26:45.888 --> 26:48.088
No, you don't understand.
Like, I have to have this job.

26:48.554 --> 26:51.721
- I get it.
- No, you don't. I mean, it's like a condition.

26:52.221 --> 26:55.263
I said I get it.
I've lived here all my life.

26:55.888 --> 26:57.221
I know
what a parole condition is,

26:57.388 --> 26:59.388
and I know
where black-and-gray tattoos

26:59.554 --> 27:01.388
with shitty ballpoint ink
get done.

27:02.013 --> 27:03.054
Ellsworth, right?

27:04.471 --> 27:05.871
I mean, I'm hoping
it was Ellsworth.

27:07.013 --> 27:08.179
Yeah, it was.

27:08.346 --> 27:10.304
Great! So, you're not violent.

27:10.471 --> 27:12.763
Now, will you go
and get the claw bar

27:12.929 --> 27:14.888
and smash
through that wall for me?

27:17.888 --> 27:18.971
Please?

27:19.513 --> 27:20.513
[chuckles]

27:20.638 --> 27:22.554
[suspenseful music]

27:22.721 --> 27:24.763
[crickets chirping]

27:25.679 --> 27:26.763
- [click]
- [grunts]

27:31.471 --> 27:32.554
- [click]
- [rattling]

27:33.388 --> 27:35.971
[beeping]

27:42.388 --> 27:43.388
[beep]

27:43.804 --> 27:45.513
[line ringing]

27:46.513 --> 27:50.596
- [woman on phone]Go <i>ahead.</i>
- 0474. Blue indigo. What's up?

27:50.763 --> 27:53.280
We're <i>getting a temperature-breach
alert from a decommissioned facility</i>

27:53.304 --> 27:55.554
<i>in the Atchison mines
in eastern Kansas.</i>

27:57.638 --> 28:00.804
Yeah. I wondered about that,
given the weather changes.

28:00.971 --> 28:04.888
I wrote a memo in 2007
on that very subject.

28:05.054 --> 28:06.721
<i>I don't</i> see <i>it in the file.</i>

28:06.888 --> 28:09.221
And I called
about five years after that.

28:09.388 --> 28:12.679
And again two years ago.
What time did the alert come in?

28:12.846 --> 28:16.554
<i>- 3:14 p.m. Central Standard Time.</i>
- And you're just calling me now?

28:16.721 --> 28:18.441
<i>It took some time
to figure out who to call.</i>

28:18.596 --> 28:20.471
[dramatic music]

28:20.638 --> 28:23.763
Okay. I'm 73 miles
from Seymour Johnson.

28:23.929 --> 28:27.513
- I can be there in 90 minutes. I need a plane from there...
- [indistinct chatter]

28:27.679 --> 28:29.763
<i>and a car
waiting on the other end.</i>

28:29.929 --> 28:32.429
Is it your opinion this qualifies
as a Heightened Threat?

28:32.596 --> 28:37.471
My opinion is it qualified as an
Exceptional Threat at 3:14 p.m.

28:37.638 --> 28:40.679
<i>-I'll</i> see <i>what I can do about
transportation</i>... -I'm not finished.

28:40.846 --> 28:43.638
I don't have any equipment.
I need everything on the list.

28:43.804 --> 28:48.138
- I'm sorry, <i>Mr.</i> Quinn, I'm just not familiar with...
- I <i>wrote an ECI white paper</i>

28:48.304 --> 28:52.763
in 2009. It's compartmented
and stored in a clean vault.

28:53.346 --> 28:56.679
Read the report and have
everything listed in Appendix A

28:56.846 --> 29:00.429
in the car in Kansas
when I land. Understood?

29:00.596 --> 29:03.013
I can't do all that
without multiple authorizations.

29:03.179 --> 29:06.304
[Robert] <i>Listen to me. This
fungus is intensely adaptable.</i>

29:06.471 --> 29:09.596
<i>It will mutate and spread
in unpredictable ways.</i>

29:09.763 --> 29:12.638
Get Gordon Gray to clear you.
Only Gordon Gray.

29:12.804 --> 29:14.138
<i>Don't call anyone else.</i>

29:16.554 --> 29:18.388
- What's your name?
<i>- You know we can't give</i>

29:18.554 --> 29:20.114
<i>that kind of information out</i>
over <i>the phone.</i>

29:20.138 --> 29:21.138
Just your first one,

29:21.679 --> 29:22.721
even a fake one,

29:23.846 --> 29:24.888
something to call you.

29:25.054 --> 29:26.554
[music continues]

29:26.721 --> 29:27.721
Abigail.

29:27.846 --> 29:29.096
[Robert]
<i>Okay, Abigail.</i>

29:30.263 --> 29:32.429
<i>Remember those good grades
you got in high school?</i>

29:33.096 --> 29:35.221
<i>And the sports
you trained your ass off for?</i>

29:35.929 --> 29:37.846
The college you fought
to get into?

29:39.054 --> 29:42.471
Remember the abuse you put up
with your first year in the department?

29:43.304 --> 29:46.513
<i>And the personal life you've
given up for the last, I don't know,</i>

29:47.054 --> 29:50.471
from your voice, it sounds
like maybe ten, 12 years now?

29:51.221 --> 29:54.471
- Nine.
<i>- Nine. All those sacrifices,</i>

29:54.638 --> 29:57.304
all the shit you've had to eat
because you wanted to do

29:57.471 --> 29:59.013
what was right for your country.

30:00.096 --> 30:01.346
This is what it was for.

30:02.221 --> 30:04.221
<i>It's worse than you can
possibly imagine.</i>

30:05.096 --> 30:08.138
We are at Pucker Factor Ten,
Abigail.

30:09.096 --> 30:11.179
But you and I are gonna
sort this shit.

30:12.179 --> 30:13.179
Sounds good?

30:15.638 --> 30:16.638
Yes.

30:17.721 --> 30:19.929
- Yes, sir.
- Get the stuff on the list.

30:20.929 --> 30:22.638
I'll be at Seymour
in 90 minutes.

30:22.804 --> 30:23.929
[crashing]

30:24.096 --> 30:26.179
[dinging]

30:26.346 --> 30:27.346
[clack]

30:28.638 --> 30:30.429
[Teacake] A whole
bunch of stuff back here.

30:31.679 --> 30:33.221
[clattering and clanking]

30:33.763 --> 30:34.763
Sorry.

30:36.096 --> 30:38.656
- [Naomi] What's that say?
- [Teacake] I gotta get a closer look.

30:38.804 --> 30:41.679
- [clattering]
- Sorry.

30:43.096 --> 30:44.929
[grunts and pants]

30:45.096 --> 30:49.179
Huh. "NTC. Thermistor Breach."

30:49.888 --> 30:51.513
Huh. Hold on, give me a second.

30:52.304 --> 30:53.388
[gasps]

30:53.554 --> 30:54.679
- [thud]
- [groaning]

30:54.846 --> 30:56.126
[Naomi]
Oh, my God! Are you okay?

30:56.471 --> 30:59.138
[coughs] Yep! Planned that.

30:59.804 --> 31:01.304
Whoa...

31:02.471 --> 31:04.513
[suspenseful tone]

31:05.888 --> 31:08.346
"Airtight Integrity," yeah,

31:08.513 --> 31:11.471
"plus or minus
0.1 degree Celsius."

31:13.054 --> 31:16.179
"Cold Chain Synchronicity."
Jesus, there's, like, 20 of them.

31:17.179 --> 31:18.739
But that's the only one
that's blinking.

31:18.763 --> 31:21.888
- "NTC. Thermistor Breach."
- What's it do?

31:22.346 --> 31:25.054
Well, a thermistor is part
of an electrical circuit.

31:25.221 --> 31:27.638
There are two kinds,
the positive kind

31:27.804 --> 31:29.763
where resistance rises
with temperature,

31:29.929 --> 31:32.263
and the negative kind
where the resistance falls

31:32.429 --> 31:33.679
when the temperature goes up.

31:34.679 --> 31:36.554
So, like a thermometer?

31:36.721 --> 31:40.346
Um, no, like a circuit
that's reactive to temperature.

31:41.846 --> 31:43.721
- Like a thermometer?
- It's not a thermometer.

31:44.763 --> 31:46.221
What? Are you
all science-y and shit?

31:46.388 --> 31:48.179
Well, I wouldn't say,
"and shit."

31:48.346 --> 31:51.596
I take a lot of science,
prerequisite for vet school.

31:53.554 --> 31:54.554
Huh.

31:57.096 --> 31:58.096
Whoa.

32:02.096 --> 32:05.679
-[thudding] -Oh! Hey!
Wha... what are you doing?

32:05.846 --> 32:07.679
- [clattering]
- [Naomi loudly exhales]

32:08.471 --> 32:10.679
[laughs] That was fun.
Oh, my God.

32:11.388 --> 32:14.513
- Oh! Oh, cool!
- [pants]

32:18.429 --> 32:19.721
Yeah, this place was a...

32:20.638 --> 32:22.388
It was military storage
back in the day,

32:22.888 --> 32:24.179
weapons and what have you.

32:24.888 --> 32:27.096
They cleaned it out
and sold it a long time ago.

32:27.763 --> 32:32.513
Storage is only on the
ground floor and two sub-levels.

32:32.679 --> 32:34.439
[Naomi] But this lab is
what they care about.

32:34.554 --> 32:37.638
See the sensors? They're all
in bunches down here,

32:37.804 --> 32:40.804
- the lower sub-basements.
- [Teacake] "SB-4."

32:41.638 --> 32:44.304
- You wanna go down and see it?
- [laughs]

32:46.513 --> 32:47.513
No.

32:48.679 --> 32:50.513
Ho... how? I mean,
they sealed it off.

32:51.429 --> 32:52.429
That.

32:53.429 --> 32:54.429
It's a tube ladder.

32:56.013 --> 32:58.804
- I'm not going down there.
- Oh, come on! This is, like,

32:58.971 --> 33:00.596
the most fun I've had in years.

33:00.763 --> 33:03.138
This is like a night out for me.
This is great.

33:03.304 --> 33:05.971
Jesus. That's depressing.

33:06.138 --> 33:07.721
- Okay.
- What, you don't go out?

33:07.888 --> 33:10.138
[deeply exhale] Not really.

33:10.304 --> 33:11.763
What about for, like, a beer?

33:12.721 --> 33:13.804
I don't drink.

33:16.221 --> 33:17.346
Not even for one beer?

33:18.263 --> 33:19.346
That would be drinking.

33:19.513 --> 33:21.554
[suspenseful music]

33:24.888 --> 33:26.013
[camera shutter clicks]

33:26.596 --> 33:28.196
- You know what? [clears throat]
- [ding]

33:28.221 --> 33:29.501
I thought you were fun, Teacake.

33:29.596 --> 33:31.138
- You started out fun.
- Who, me?

33:31.304 --> 33:34.013
- [grunts]
- Oh, I'm fun. Oh, I'm huge fun.

33:34.471 --> 33:37.530
You're the one... you just said your best night
out in years is vandalizing your workplace.

33:37.554 --> 33:39.679
And that's cool, and I'm,
I'm, like, cooperating.

33:39.846 --> 33:41.322
You look at me with those eyes
you got and say, "Please,

33:41.346 --> 33:43.471
smash a hole in the wall,"
I'm on board.

33:43.638 --> 33:46.438
And then you say, "Let's crawl into
this weird space and check it out."

33:46.596 --> 33:48.013
Still good, I'm into it.

33:48.179 --> 33:49.763
But then, you come at me, like,

33:49.929 --> 33:52.013
"Go crawl down the tube ladder
a couple hundred feet

33:52.179 --> 33:54.072
into the blocked-off part
of the abandoned government shit

33:54.096 --> 33:56.013
and see why the thermistor alarm
is going off,"

33:56.179 --> 33:58.388
and a guy's just gotta
take a second to, like,

33:58.554 --> 34:00.429
think things through,
you feel me?

34:01.888 --> 34:03.013
You like my eyes?

34:04.596 --> 34:06.679
- Y... yeah, in fact, I do.
- [clicks]

34:07.429 --> 34:11.429
- That's very sweet.
- My point is I'm kinda easy to...

34:12.346 --> 34:15.054
talk into things, and that's
why I got the problems I got,

34:15.221 --> 34:16.989
but I spend a lot of time
working on my personal shit,

34:17.013 --> 34:18.679
so I don't just walk
into everything

34:18.846 --> 34:20.280
that everybody asks me to do
all the time,

34:20.304 --> 34:21.624
which is what I'm doing
right now.

34:21.721 --> 34:23.388
All right?
I'm just taking a little...

34:24.179 --> 34:25.221
A moment.

34:27.013 --> 34:29.513
- Okay.
- [deeply breathes]

34:29.679 --> 34:32.888
Word of advice,
if a guy who goes by Hazy Davy

34:33.054 --> 34:35.094
ever asks you to wait
behind the wheel while he runs

34:35.179 --> 34:37.405
in the convenience store real
quick, you should for sure remember

34:37.429 --> 34:39.388
you got something else to do
right away, okay?

34:41.513 --> 34:42.679
I'm sorry.

34:43.346 --> 34:45.388
I... I was not being cool.

34:46.763 --> 34:48.304
That's more like it. [chuckle]

34:53.179 --> 34:54.304
[ding]

34:54.846 --> 34:56.221
You coming or what?

34:56.388 --> 34:57.221
[giggles]

34:57.304 --> 34:58.971
[whimsical tone]

34:59.138 --> 35:00.138
[elevator chimes]

35:03.638 --> 35:05.679
You think that picture's
gonna cover that hole?

35:06.804 --> 35:07.804
Yeah, it'll be fine!

35:08.721 --> 35:09.739
[elevator voice]
<i>Going down.</i>

35:09.763 --> 35:11.679
[ominous music]

35:11.846 --> 35:13.888
- [crickets chirping]
- [engine rumbling]

35:36.638 --> 35:38.804
[engine revving]

35:53.138 --> 35:54.638
[grunting]

36:02.429 --> 36:04.109
-[chiming] -[elevator
voice] <i>Sub-level two.</i>

36:05.013 --> 36:07.388
[clacking]

36:08.263 --> 36:09.638
[Naomi]
Okay.

36:13.263 --> 36:14.263
I think it's this way.

36:15.388 --> 36:16.596
What, so the janitor's closet?

36:16.763 --> 36:18.388
Uh, that doesn't make sense.

36:21.888 --> 36:24.114
The only person who comes in here
is Dave, and he's a horrible janitor,

36:24.138 --> 36:25.846
- so he's never in here.
- That's weird,

36:26.013 --> 36:27.888
it's supposed to go
50 feet that way.

36:30.054 --> 36:31.346
[Teacake]
Is that an outline?

36:32.304 --> 36:34.096
- [thuds]
- [gasping]

36:34.263 --> 36:36.304
- [wind blowing]
- [soft rustling]

36:37.554 --> 36:38.554
Now, that was cool.

36:39.513 --> 36:40.971
- Thanks.
- [clicks]

36:41.138 --> 36:43.263
- [clanks]
- [suspenseful music]

36:46.054 --> 36:47.054
[clicks]

36:48.888 --> 36:51.388
- [whistles]
- [Naomi] Oh, this is crazy! D...

36:51.554 --> 36:53.474
Do you think we're gonna get
in trouble for this?

36:53.554 --> 36:54.638
[blows raspberries]

36:55.679 --> 36:56.846
[Teacake]
Probably.

36:57.388 --> 36:58.721
- [crackling]
- Oh!

37:00.888 --> 37:04.179
[loudly exhales] I mean,
there's an alarm going off.

37:06.013 --> 37:07.721
Who they gonna call,
the cops? No.

37:07.888 --> 37:10.263
Call Griffin? Absolutely not.

37:10.888 --> 37:12.929
Plus, he crunk as shit
by now, dog.

37:13.096 --> 37:15.388
- Why do you talk like that?
- Like what?

37:15.554 --> 37:17.263
Like you're from the hood.

37:17.929 --> 37:19.471
Everybody I know
talks like this.

37:19.638 --> 37:21.888
Well, you know me now,
and I don't talk like that.

37:22.054 --> 37:23.864
[Teacake] Yeah, that's
'cause you're all smart and shit

37:23.888 --> 37:25.280
with your science
and your vet school

37:25.304 --> 37:26.679
and your general what-have-you.

37:27.304 --> 37:29.304
You know what you are?
Loquacious.

37:30.054 --> 37:31.763
- "Loquacious"? [sharply blows]
- Mm-hmm.

37:32.929 --> 37:33.971
Yeah, I like that.

37:34.679 --> 37:36.721
It's like some detective movie
from the '70s.

37:37.679 --> 37:38.888
"Loquacious Jackson,

37:40.013 --> 37:41.804
he ain't bringing
anybody home alive."

37:41.971 --> 37:44.971
You ever see <i>Foxy Brown?</i>
Man, that movie is the shit!

37:45.471 --> 37:48.263
When she pulls the gun out of her
hair? Oh, that part was so classic.

37:48.429 --> 37:51.054
What's that mean by the way,
"loquacious"?

37:51.221 --> 37:52.721
Talking is easy for you.

37:55.054 --> 37:56.596
- Yeah, I guess so.
- [chuckles]

37:57.388 --> 37:58.888
[Naomi]
So, what's your real name?

38:00.054 --> 38:01.388
[Teacake]
Uh, Travis.

38:02.221 --> 38:03.679
Travis!

38:03.846 --> 38:05.638
That's a nice name,
you should use it more.

38:09.013 --> 38:11.138
How do you think you'd pee
in one of these things?

38:11.304 --> 38:14.763
- I have no idea.
- Like a little, uh... [whistles]

38:17.763 --> 38:19.471
So, where does
your nickname come from?

38:20.929 --> 38:23.138
- I don't know you well enough.
- [scoffs]

38:23.304 --> 38:24.846
- [light clicks]
- [suspenseful tone]

38:25.013 --> 38:26.929
[Naomi chuckling]
There it is! It's here!

38:27.096 --> 38:29.054
Oh, my God! [laughs] That's it!

38:29.513 --> 38:30.346
The tube ladder!

38:30.429 --> 38:32.179
[groan] Great!

38:33.346 --> 38:35.888
- [clang]
- [loud creaking]

38:36.054 --> 38:37.596
[panting]

38:37.763 --> 38:39.239
-[Naomi softly] Okay.
Okay. [grunts] -[grunts]

38:39.263 --> 38:41.513
[rattling]

38:45.013 --> 38:46.138
Jesus...

38:46.888 --> 38:48.929
[ominous music]

38:50.263 --> 38:51.263
[Naomi]
Whoa.

38:52.054 --> 38:53.429
[Teacake]
Holy shit!

38:53.596 --> 38:55.179
[clanking]

38:55.346 --> 38:56.679
How far down
do you think it goes?

38:58.263 --> 39:01.721
I don't know, at least 400,
maybe 500 feet?

39:02.929 --> 39:06.013
- [loudly] Hey! [echoes]
- [Naomi softly] Oh, my God.

39:08.013 --> 39:09.971
Okay. So,
you're going down first.

39:12.846 --> 39:15.054
Okay. [grunts]

39:16.721 --> 39:18.013
[Naomi]
Good luck!

39:21.221 --> 39:23.304
[Teacake grunting]

39:23.471 --> 39:25.013
[dramatic tone]

39:25.179 --> 39:27.304
- [crickets chirping]
- [line ringing]

39:27.471 --> 39:29.239
[Mike] Ridiculous
bullshit I gotta put up with

39:29.263 --> 39:30.971
from this woman, I swear to God.

39:31.471 --> 39:33.614
[Naomi on voicemail] <i>Hi, this is
Naomi. Please leave a message.</i>

39:33.638 --> 39:34.971
- [beep]
- Hi, honey.

39:36.263 --> 39:37.888
Uh, it's me. Well...

39:39.304 --> 39:40.513
This is what happens.

39:42.013 --> 39:44.294
You know, you don't talk to
someone, they've got no choice

39:44.346 --> 39:47.513
but to show up at your place of
work, I mean, it's just what happens.

39:48.471 --> 39:50.429
Okay, look,
I've got a problem, okay?

39:50.971 --> 39:52.614
And I can't go home
and I don't know what to do

39:52.638 --> 39:54.013
and the problem is that...

39:54.929 --> 39:57.596
The problem is,
um, it's in my trunk.

39:59.263 --> 40:01.888
Okay? And I'm here now,
and my trunk is here, obviously,

40:02.471 --> 40:03.929
and I need your help.

40:04.096 --> 40:05.263
So, I'm coming in.

40:06.804 --> 40:09.054
-I'm coming in. [shakily
breathes] -[beeps]

40:14.429 --> 40:15.429
[muffled thud]

40:15.471 --> 40:17.513
[suspenseful music]

40:19.554 --> 40:21.846
[muffled thudding]

40:29.304 --> 40:30.346
[whimpers]

40:36.388 --> 40:38.013
[thudding]

40:38.888 --> 40:39.888
[groans]

40:44.513 --> 40:45.804
[groans]

40:50.596 --> 40:52.221
- [thud and clack]
- [gasps]

40:53.679 --> 40:55.304
No. No, you're dead.

40:55.929 --> 40:57.554
You're dead,
you're supposed to be dead!

40:59.804 --> 41:00.929
<i>Mr.</i> Scroggins?

41:04.221 --> 41:05.388
<i>Mr.</i> Scroggins?

41:10.304 --> 41:11.804
[music increases]

41:11.971 --> 41:13.721
[snarling]

41:13.888 --> 41:17.054
[crying] <i>Mr.</i> Scrogg...
You're alive! [shakily laughs]

41:17.221 --> 41:19.013
Listen, I'm so sorry
I shot you, man.

41:19.179 --> 41:21.096
- [snarling]
- But you're okay!

41:21.263 --> 41:22.721
[growling and hissing]

41:23.179 --> 41:24.179
[Mike shrieks]

41:24.221 --> 41:26.263
[hissing and growling]

41:28.846 --> 41:30.971
<i>- [Mr.</i> Scroggins barfing]
- What the hell?

41:31.721 --> 41:33.221
<i>[Mr.</i> Scroggins meowing]

41:34.179 --> 41:36.513
- [meowing and hissing]
- What happened to you?

41:38.304 --> 41:40.054
- [yowl]
<i>- Mr.</i> Scroggins, come here!

41:40.763 --> 41:42.804
<i>Mr.</i> Scroggins...
Come here! [stutters]

41:42.971 --> 41:44.771
-[meowing] -No, no,
no, no! Don't go up there!

41:44.846 --> 41:47.138
[panting]

41:47.304 --> 41:49.846
- [meows]
- [clinking]

41:51.346 --> 41:53.346
[meowing]

41:55.179 --> 41:56.763
- [flesh squelching]
- [Mike groans]

42:00.429 --> 42:02.346
- [explosion and splattering]
- [groans]

42:02.513 --> 42:03.804
[bellowing]

42:07.304 --> 42:09.221
- [belches]
- [whooshing]

42:09.388 --> 42:11.429
[tense music]

42:15.471 --> 42:17.929
[panting]

42:19.138 --> 42:20.763
So, is your kid a boy or a girl?

42:21.429 --> 42:23.638
[Naomi]
A... girl.

42:24.513 --> 42:25.513
Huh.

42:26.263 --> 42:29.263
- Name?
- Sarah. She's six.

42:30.679 --> 42:33.346
You're pretty young,
you know, for, like, a kid.

42:33.513 --> 42:34.513
Okay.

42:36.054 --> 42:38.471
- Did you think twice about that?
- Uh, having her?

42:39.096 --> 42:41.429
- Yeah.
- Yeah, of course, I was 18.

42:41.596 --> 42:42.679
You regret it?

42:44.638 --> 42:46.679
Sorry, is that, like,
a messed-up thing to say?

42:47.304 --> 42:50.179
No, it's... real,
like, really real.

42:50.929 --> 42:53.721
- Most guys don't ask about her.
- Huh.

42:54.304 --> 42:56.239
Well, I, I don't mean to get
all personal or anything.

42:56.263 --> 42:57.554
- That's okay.
- [alarm blares]

42:57.721 --> 42:59.638
[whimsical, suspenseful music]

42:59.804 --> 43:02.513
[buzzing]

43:03.096 --> 43:06.054
[Teacake]
"DTRA. Access only."

43:06.221 --> 43:08.679
Man, I sure would like to know
what those letters stand for.

43:08.846 --> 43:12.596
What if it's "Don't touch,
radiation, asshole?"

43:12.763 --> 43:15.013
You know,
that would be some amusing shit.

43:15.721 --> 43:18.804
You know, I'm, I'm cool
with going back up if you want.

43:21.179 --> 43:22.346
[scoffs]

43:23.721 --> 43:25.846
[grunting]

43:26.013 --> 43:28.221
- [creaking]
- [alarm blares]

43:28.388 --> 43:30.638
[grunting continues]

43:34.429 --> 43:36.388
[creaking]

43:40.138 --> 43:41.429
- You got it?
- Yeah.

43:44.804 --> 43:47.096
- [clang]
- [grunting] It's actually...

43:47.263 --> 43:49.763
[panting]
lighter than I thought.

43:54.096 --> 43:55.263
[alarm blares]

43:55.429 --> 43:57.346
[suspenseful music]

43:57.513 --> 43:59.346
[water running]

43:59.513 --> 44:00.554
Huh.

44:02.804 --> 44:03.804
That's weird.

44:04.304 --> 44:05.346
[alarm blares]

44:10.971 --> 44:12.304
- Oh.
- [Naomi] Hot?

44:13.179 --> 44:15.054
Cold. Freezing.

44:15.679 --> 44:20.263
That'<i>s...</i> weird, I don't hear
any... pumps or anything.

44:20.846 --> 44:22.513
Underground cold spring?

44:22.679 --> 44:24.013
I... I guess so.

44:29.304 --> 44:30.304
[alarm blares]

44:30.471 --> 44:32.054
It's coming from in there.

44:33.388 --> 44:35.054
- You wanna open it?
- Nope, I'm good.

44:35.221 --> 44:36.679
I'm good. [nervous chuckle]

44:36.846 --> 44:38.346
- [screeching]
- Wait...

44:39.388 --> 44:40.614
- [gasps]
- [Teacake] What the...

44:40.638 --> 44:42.679
[ominous music]

44:43.929 --> 44:49.596
- Ugh! Oh, it's a rat king!
- What the hell's a rat king?

44:49.763 --> 44:51.989
They wrote about them in the
Middle Ages during the plague.

44:52.013 --> 44:55.138
- They thought they were like a bad omen.
- No shit it's a bad omen.

44:55.304 --> 44:56.513
Look at this thing.

44:56.679 --> 44:58.179
How'd they get like that?

44:58.346 --> 45:01.054
Their tails get, like,
knotted and stuck together

45:01.221 --> 45:02.971
with pine sap or something.

45:03.138 --> 45:05.221
Holy shit,
that one's eating the other one.

45:06.054 --> 45:08.179
Well, this is some horrific,
repugnant shit, man.

45:08.346 --> 45:10.822
I have never seen anything
like this in my entire goddamn life,

45:10.846 --> 45:12.846
and I've seen some crazy shit,
this is fucked!

45:13.013 --> 45:16.929
It's not pine sap,
it's like a slime mold?

45:17.096 --> 45:19.197
- [hissing and screeching]
- I think you're making it angry.

45:19.221 --> 45:21.179
It's not a mold,
there's no froth,

45:21.346 --> 45:24.596
it's moving, it's,
like, fungal ooze.

45:24.763 --> 45:27.013
God, that is a lot of fungus!

45:28.221 --> 45:30.054
- [sharply exhales]
- [alarm blares]

45:32.013 --> 45:34.221
[Naomi]
What is that stuff?

45:35.554 --> 45:36.679
<i>Mm...</i>

45:37.554 --> 45:39.471
- [hissing]
- [loudly gasps]

45:39.638 --> 45:41.679
[suspenseful music]

45:43.846 --> 45:46.096
[squelching]

45:56.721 --> 45:58.179
[Teacake]
Yo, what are you doing?

46:02.721 --> 46:03.763
Naomi!

46:04.513 --> 46:06.179
- The door's hot.
- Yeah.

46:06.804 --> 46:09.888
And there's green shit coming out of
that room, there's a goddamn rat king,

46:10.054 --> 46:11.971
and curiosity is awesome
and everything,

46:12.138 --> 46:14.338
but I think it's time we get
the hell out of here, okay?

46:14.429 --> 46:15.721
- Me too.
- [alarm blares]

46:15.888 --> 46:17.447
- [sharply blowing]
- [creaking and rumbling]

46:17.471 --> 46:19.638
- Did you get any of that shit on you?
- No

46:19.804 --> 46:22.679
- You sure? Oh, great.
- No.

46:23.804 --> 46:24.804
[door slams]

46:24.888 --> 46:27.888
[vomiting and groaning]

46:28.054 --> 46:30.096
[crickets chirping]

46:33.179 --> 46:34.971
[vomiting]

46:35.138 --> 46:37.179
- [whooshing]
- [squelching]

46:38.054 --> 46:40.513
[Mike echoing] <i>Find more
people, find more people,</i>

46:40.679 --> 46:43.513
<i>find more people, find more
people, find more people...</i>

46:44.388 --> 46:45.721
[loudly] <i>find more people!</i>

46:46.554 --> 46:47.804
Gotta find Naomi.

46:49.388 --> 46:52.388
I gotta find Naomi.
[heavily breathing]

46:56.013 --> 46:58.054
[ominous music]

47:03.929 --> 47:06.596
[bellowing and snorting]

47:19.888 --> 47:21.929
[airplane rumbling]

47:22.429 --> 47:23.929
[Trini]
<i>No, Hero, stop!</i>

47:25.054 --> 47:28.096
- [Robert] <i>put it down, Hero.</i>
- [Trini]Hero, <i>you're infected! Hero!</i>

47:28.263 --> 47:30.179
- [Hero gasping]
- [Robert] <i>Don 't!</i>

47:30.346 --> 47:31.638
- No, <i>no, no, no!</i>
- [gunshot]

47:31.804 --> 47:33.429
- [telephone rings]
- [grunts]

47:37.679 --> 47:41.471
- Qué <i>pasó,</i> Abigail? I was very specific.
<i>- Ls there a problem?</i>

47:41.638 --> 47:43.679
My screen has you
over Fayetteville already.

47:43.846 --> 47:46.304
<i>You have me in a modified
command transport,</i>

47:46.471 --> 47:48.763
which means it's official
and I'm logged.

47:50.721 --> 47:53.429
There's gonna be a welcoming
committee on the other end.

47:53.596 --> 47:55.096
You didn't call Gordon Gray.

47:56.388 --> 47:58.138
Mr. Gray passed away
a year and a half ago.

47:58.304 --> 48:00.388
[melancholic music]

48:01.471 --> 48:03.471
I see. That explains a lot.

48:04.346 --> 48:07.304
<i>- I'm sorry.</i>
- Who did you call instead?

48:07.471 --> 48:09.679
Thank you, Lieutenant.
You can clear the line now.

48:09.846 --> 48:11.263
[indistinct chatter]

48:11.429 --> 48:12.429
Yes, sir.

48:12.596 --> 48:13.596
Hello, Robert.

48:14.013 --> 48:16.679
- How's the back?
- Hey, Jerabek.

48:17.138 --> 48:19.971
I thought you put this one
to bed 20 years ago.

48:20.138 --> 48:22.721
[Robert] <i>Eighteen.
Apparently, it woke up.</i>

48:22.888 --> 48:27.013
- Sounds like a broken thermistor to me.
- That would be nice to think.

48:27.179 --> 48:30.471
[Jerabek] <i>I don't share this particular
obsession of yours and Gordon's.</i>

48:30.638 --> 48:32.221
You never saw what it can do.

48:32.388 --> 48:34.554
No one has because
it's been safely contained

48:34.721 --> 48:37.513
- for 20 years.
- [Robert] <i>Till you sealed the place up and sold it.</i>

48:37.679 --> 48:39.888
It was contained. Permanently.

48:40.054 --> 48:43.138
Sure, unless Gordon died
and the climate changed

48:43.304 --> 48:45.804
and the underground spring
warmed up.

48:46.513 --> 48:48.596
Oh, shit. That all happened.

48:49.054 --> 48:52.138
I will not get sucked
into this conversation with you.

48:52.304 --> 48:55.888
You're on that airplane solely as a
gesture of respect to the old man.

48:56.429 --> 48:59.679
<i>Threat assessment and a
sober report from Atchison,</i>

48:59.846 --> 49:01.054
that's all I want.

49:01.804 --> 49:03.638
No off-the-book stuff, clear?

49:03.804 --> 49:05.388
[Robert]
<i>I'll check it out and go home.</i>

49:05.554 --> 49:07.221
Oh, and by the way,
you're welcome.

49:07.846 --> 49:10.013
I'm not exactly
on the clock anymore.

49:10.179 --> 49:12.263
You should probably take me
off the file.

49:12.429 --> 49:15.096
- Yeah, I'll do that.
- Up yours, asshole.

49:15.263 --> 49:17.304
<i>- I'm still here, Robert.</i>
- I know.

49:19.054 --> 49:20.179
[satellite phone ringing]

49:24.263 --> 49:25.263
[beep]

49:26.596 --> 49:29.721
- Abigail?
- I'm secure, on my personal cell.

49:29.888 --> 49:32.263
- I take it you read my white paper.
<i>- I did.</i>

49:32.429 --> 49:35.054
- Was it as bad as what you wrote?
<i>- It's worse, Abigail.</i>

49:35.221 --> 49:38.554
<i>And Jerabek and all the people in
power now don't understand that.</i>

49:38.721 --> 49:41.096
They would stop us from doing
what needs to be done

49:41.596 --> 49:44.221
until it's too late,
but we won't let them.

49:44.388 --> 49:47.179
- What do you need from me?
- Airplane Wi-Fi won't be secure enough

49:47.346 --> 49:49.221
for the conversations
I need to have,

49:50.179 --> 49:52.054
so you have to make
the calls for me.

49:52.638 --> 49:56.304
<i>Start with a former agent
named Trini Romano.</i>

49:56.763 --> 49:59.638
Tell her,
"Margo is under the weather."

49:59.804 --> 50:02.054
I'm not saying I, I am, Darius.

50:02.221 --> 50:03.929
I... I'm just saying I'm late.

50:05.429 --> 50:07.179
I'm... I'm really sorry,
do you mind?

50:07.346 --> 50:08.346
[softly] Excuse me.

50:08.763 --> 50:09.763
[softly chuckles]

50:10.679 --> 50:13.054
- Clear.
<i>- Trini will help you with the list,</i>

50:13.221 --> 50:14.429
even <i>item seven.</i>

50:14.888 --> 50:16.638
Especially item seven.

50:17.513 --> 50:20.429
Believe it or not, Abigail,
I've done all this before.

50:20.596 --> 50:22.096
Including item seven?

50:23.513 --> 50:24.846
Call Trini Romano.

50:26.929 --> 50:28.971
[suspenseful music]

50:29.138 --> 50:30.179
Jesus!

50:30.846 --> 50:33.138
DTRA. Defense Threat
Reduction Agency.

50:33.846 --> 50:34.846
[Teacake]
Oh.

50:36.804 --> 50:38.138
Who are these guys?

50:40.554 --> 50:44.679
- [Naomi] What the hell?
- "Pyongyang Biotoxin Briefing Notes"?

50:44.846 --> 50:46.554
- Oh, my God.
- I know.

50:49.429 --> 50:51.888
[huffing]

50:58.096 --> 50:59.596
- [Naomi] Travis.
- What?

51:00.846 --> 51:02.013
What's going on?

51:02.888 --> 51:04.804
Holy shit.

51:06.263 --> 51:07.596
- [deer grunts]
- I...

51:08.846 --> 51:10.013
am confused.

51:10.179 --> 51:12.054
- [Naomi] Huh.
- [elevator chimes]

51:13.804 --> 51:15.221
[deer grunts]

51:19.513 --> 51:21.596
That fucking deer
just took the fucking elevator.

51:21.763 --> 51:23.304
[bellowing]

51:24.138 --> 51:25.971
- [scoffs]
- How does that even happen?

51:26.804 --> 51:28.846
[squelching]

51:29.596 --> 51:32.054
-["One Way or Another" by
Blondie] -[glass shattering]

51:47.388 --> 51:51.096
♪ <i>One way or another
I'm gonna find ya</i> ♪

51:51.263 --> 51:53.096
♪ <i>I'm gonna get ya, get ya
get ya, get ya</i> ♪

51:53.263 --> 51:57.013
♪ <i>One way or another
I'm gonna win ya</i> ♪

51:57.179 --> 51:59.054
♪ <i>I'm gonna get ya, get ya
get ya, get ya</i> ♪

51:59.221 --> 52:02.929
♪ <i>One way or another
I'm gonna</i> see <i>ya</i> ♪

52:03.096 --> 52:04.936
♪ <i>I'm gonna meet ya, meet ya</i>
meet <i>ya, meet ya</i> ♪

52:05.096 --> 52:07.429
- [rat screeching]
- ♪ <i>One way maybe next week</i> ♪

52:07.596 --> 52:10.971
♪ <i>I'm gonna meet ya I'm
gonna meet ya I'll meet ya</i> ♪

52:11.138 --> 52:17.013
♪ <i>I will drive past your house</i> ♪

52:17.179 --> 52:22.513
♪ <i>And if the lights
are all down</i> ♪

52:22.679 --> 52:26.346
- ♪ <i>I'll</i> see <i>who's around...</i> ♪
- [Rooney] Fifty-two years...

52:33.429 --> 52:35.846
♪ <i>One way or another</i> ♪

52:36.013 --> 52:39.263
♪ <i>I'm gonna get ya, I'll get ya
I'll get ya, get ya get ya, get ya</i> ♪

52:39.429 --> 52:41.721
♪ <i>One way or another</i> ♪

52:41.888 --> 52:43.554
♪ <i>I'm gonna get ya
I'll get ya</i> ♪

52:43.721 --> 52:45.763
♪ <i>I'll get ya, get ya
get ya, get ya, one</i>... ♪

52:45.929 --> 52:47.846
[crickets chirping]

52:48.013 --> 52:50.054
[squelching]

52:54.846 --> 52:56.888
[ominous music]

52:59.929 --> 53:01.013
[yowling]

53:01.638 --> 53:04.638
Whoever DTRA is,
we gotta call 'em, like, now.

53:04.804 --> 53:06.763
- [elevator voice] <i>Going up.</i>
- [bellow]

53:07.638 --> 53:09.489
- Get out of here and then call them? Mm-hmm.
- Yeah, stairs.

53:09.513 --> 53:11.554
[music increases]

53:13.138 --> 53:15.388
[panting]

53:15.554 --> 53:17.554
That's, like,
some seriously upsetting shit.

53:21.138 --> 53:22.929
- [deer bellowing]
- [shouts] Oh, there...

53:27.429 --> 53:29.471
[deer groaning]

53:32.888 --> 53:34.763
[cracking]

53:34.929 --> 53:38.096
[softly] That's not natural.

53:38.263 --> 53:39.804
- [snorting]
- Uh-oh.

53:42.971 --> 53:44.471
- [bellow]
- [cracking]

53:47.763 --> 53:50.221
- [explosion]
- [splattering]

53:50.888 --> 53:51.888
[gasps]

53:52.304 --> 53:54.263
- [panting]
- [squelching]

53:55.096 --> 53:57.554
[ominous music]

54:00.346 --> 54:01.846
- Thank you.
- Uh-huh.

54:06.179 --> 54:07.971
- [elevator chimes]
- [Mike] Honey?

54:08.138 --> 54:09.138
Mike?

54:10.013 --> 54:11.013
Hi.

54:11.721 --> 54:12.721
Hi.

54:13.679 --> 54:17.221
- Yo, you were in the elevator with that thing?
- [wheezing]

54:18.638 --> 54:20.471
Are you okay, man?

54:21.096 --> 54:23.554
- I shot Mr. Scroggins.
- [Naomi] You what?

54:23.721 --> 54:25.221
Wait, who the hell
is <i>Mr.</i> Scroggins?

54:25.388 --> 54:26.989
Oh, it's his parents' cat.
I love that cat.

54:27.013 --> 54:28.888
What is wrong with you?
Why would you do that?

54:29.054 --> 54:31.155
I didn't know it was loaded
and then I thought he was dead,

54:31.179 --> 54:34.304
but he blew up,
now he's green stuff. [laughs]

54:34.471 --> 54:36.263
- So, this is Dad, huh?
- Shut up.

54:36.429 --> 54:38.846
- [wheezing]
- [teeth clack]

54:39.013 --> 54:40.263
Open your mouth.

54:40.429 --> 54:42.054
I wanna throw up in it.

54:42.846 --> 54:44.263
- What?
- [Mike] Open...

54:44.888 --> 54:47.888
- your... [shouts] mouths!
- [Teacake] Uh-oh.

54:48.054 --> 54:49.971
- [gunshot]
- [screaming]

54:50.138 --> 54:51.346
[gasps]

54:51.513 --> 54:54.013
What in the name
of heaven's glory?

54:54.179 --> 54:56.596
- [panting]
- [dramatic music]

54:56.763 --> 54:59.596
- Oh, Jesus...
- [Mike yelling] Naomi!

55:00.638 --> 55:03.013
- Naomi!
- [Teacake] This way, come on, come on!

55:04.054 --> 55:06.596
- This way! This way!
- [yelling]

55:06.763 --> 55:07.929
[Teacake groaning]

55:08.096 --> 55:09.304
[Mike distantly]
Naomi!

55:10.138 --> 55:11.388
Where are you?

55:12.554 --> 55:14.596
[wheezing]

55:16.554 --> 55:17.554
[softly] Shit.

55:20.054 --> 55:21.197
- [Naomi] This way, this way!
- Okay!

55:21.221 --> 55:22.638
[Mike]
Naomi!

55:22.804 --> 55:24.638
[indistinct yelling]

55:24.804 --> 55:27.638
Oh! Oh, God. Uh... [groans]

55:28.513 --> 55:31.721
- [Mike yelling]
- [groans] Come on!

55:34.388 --> 55:35.447
- [Teacake grunts]
- Come on!

55:35.471 --> 55:36.471
[Mike]
Where are you?

55:36.513 --> 55:37.513
[rattling]

55:38.679 --> 55:40.346
- Naomi!
- [Naomi] Close it!

55:40.513 --> 55:41.554
[rattling]

55:41.721 --> 55:42.971
[Teacake muffled]
It's jammed!

55:44.263 --> 55:45.096
[shushes]

55:45.221 --> 55:47.138
[Mike wheezing]

55:47.304 --> 55:49.346
[suspenseful music]

55:56.388 --> 55:58.179
[mouthing]

55:59.846 --> 56:01.763
[teeth clacking]

56:01.929 --> 56:03.971
[wheezing]

56:10.638 --> 56:11.679
[clattering]

56:22.971 --> 56:25.013
- [wheezing]
- [teeth clacking]

56:25.804 --> 56:27.596
[Mike yells]
Naomi!

56:29.846 --> 56:32.096
[shakily breathes, sighs]

56:38.096 --> 56:40.429
[cymbals crashing]

56:42.804 --> 56:45.221
[wobbling]

57:03.596 --> 57:05.638
- [rattling]
- [yelling]

57:06.846 --> 57:08.679
- [crunch]
- [Mike shouts]

57:10.596 --> 57:12.138
[groaning]

57:12.304 --> 57:16.221
Um, uh, DTRA has a number
for a place called Fort Belvoir.

57:16.388 --> 57:18.530
- Yeah, yeah, it's a military base.
- So, do I call them?

57:18.554 --> 57:20.304
- Or do I call the cops?
- [Mike yells]

57:20.471 --> 57:22.221
[banging]

57:22.388 --> 57:24.429
- [yelling]
- Call the fucking Army.

57:24.596 --> 57:25.429
[Naomi]
Okay.

57:25.513 --> 57:27.429
[engine rumbling]

57:27.596 --> 57:29.638
[light suspenseful music]

57:36.054 --> 57:38.096
[coughing]

57:38.263 --> 57:40.138
How's it possible
you're still alive?

57:40.638 --> 57:43.888
- Too mean to die.
- Sexy ride. Very practical.

57:44.054 --> 57:45.138
Don't even start.

57:46.804 --> 57:48.096
Yep, it's all there.

57:48.263 --> 57:49.679
Including item seven?

57:51.179 --> 57:53.804
No, we, uh, we have
to pick that one up.

57:54.804 --> 57:55.929
Are you kidding me?

57:56.471 --> 57:58.513
[light dramatic music]

58:02.888 --> 58:04.054
[line ringing]

58:06.513 --> 58:07.763
- [beep]
- Abigail?

58:07.929 --> 58:09.929
We got a call
from inside Atchison.

58:10.096 --> 58:12.346
<i>- Who?</i>
- Civilian, 24-year-old woman.

58:12.513 --> 58:15.679
- How'd she get your number?
- She googled DTRA off a door

58:15.846 --> 58:17.388
and called the emergency number.

58:17.554 --> 58:19.179
Okay, she's no dummy. Good.

58:19.346 --> 58:21.138
I have her on the other line
on the burner.

58:21.304 --> 58:22.596
- You want her?
- Yes.

58:22.763 --> 58:24.554
<i>Hang on. Her name's Naomi.</i>

58:25.429 --> 58:27.471
Civilian, inside the facility.

58:29.429 --> 58:31.304
I hope she's enjoyed
a full life.

58:31.471 --> 58:34.304
- [Mike yelling]
- [banging]

58:34.471 --> 58:36.429
Hello, Naomi. My name is Robert.

58:36.596 --> 58:38.155
Ask him what in the name
of Christ is going on!

58:38.179 --> 58:39.929
<i>I hear someone else
there with you.</i>

58:40.096 --> 58:42.429
Could you please ask him
to shut the fuck up?

58:42.596 --> 58:45.346
- What's he saying?
- Travis, can you please shut the fuck up?

58:45.513 --> 58:47.513
Okay, um, we have
a real problem here.

58:47.679 --> 58:49.888
<i>There's, like,
a virus or, or a fungus...</i>

58:50.054 --> 58:51.513
Correct on the second one.

58:51.679 --> 58:53.763
I know all about it.
Are you somewhere safe?

58:53.929 --> 58:56.013
Uh, we're... we're, uh,
locked in a storage unit.

58:56.179 --> 58:59.846
Stay there. Has anyone come into
direct physical contact with the fungus?

59:00.388 --> 59:03.221
- [Mike shouts]
- At least one person.

59:03.388 --> 59:05.280
- [Teacake] The deer! Tell him about the deer!
- [Naomi mumbles] ...deer!

59:05.304 --> 59:07.263
The deer! Um, th...
There was a deer,

59:07.429 --> 59:09.888
- and it was infected and it, it blew up.
- [mimics explosion]

59:10.054 --> 59:12.155
- Inside or outside?
- I'm sorry, did you hear what I just said?

59:12.179 --> 59:15.888
- I said it blew up.
<i>- I heard you. And I asked where.</i>

59:16.054 --> 59:17.929
- In the hallway.
- [banging]

59:18.096 --> 59:20.096
<i>Yeah, that means
it didn't try to climb,</i>

59:20.263 --> 59:22.679
<i>so it's adapting,
finding new ways to spread.</i>

59:23.179 --> 59:25.804
Okay, listen, Naomi.
You called the right people.

59:25.971 --> 59:28.429
Some of us have encountered
this situation before.

59:28.596 --> 59:31.679
Stay put, do you hear me? Do
not let it make contact with your skin.

59:31.846 --> 59:33.721
And do not call anyone else.

59:33.888 --> 59:36.221
<i>Speak only to Abigail</i>
or <i>to me, Naomi.</i>

59:36.388 --> 59:38.096
<i>- Understand?</i>
- I understand.

59:38.679 --> 59:41.119
<i>- Keep Travis calm.</i>
- I heard my name. Is he talking about me?

59:41.221 --> 59:43.263
He <i>sounds like the type
who might try to run.</i>

59:43.429 --> 59:46.971
Don't let him. 40 minutes.
You're gonna be fine.

59:47.138 --> 59:49.346
<i>- I promise.</i>
- [Mike groaning and wheezing]

59:51.971 --> 59:54.471
We're gonna be fine!
We're gonna be fine.

59:55.638 --> 59:58.138
They're gonna die, aren't they?

59:58.804 --> 59:59.804
Probably.

59:59.846 --> 01:00:01.888
[dramatic tone]

01:00:03.138 --> 01:00:04.679
[wheezing]

01:00:05.888 --> 01:00:09.138
- It's, like, some zombie shit.
- Zombies are not real.

01:00:11.054 --> 01:00:13.054
- Zombies are real.
- [Mike growling]

01:00:13.221 --> 01:00:16.096
- Zombies are 100% real.
- No, they're not, Travis.

01:00:16.263 --> 01:00:18.471
It's, like, movies, TV shows.

01:00:18.638 --> 01:00:21.598
Yes, and some really fucking excellent
TV and movies I'd like to point out,

01:00:21.721 --> 01:00:23.201
but that's not
what I'm talking about.

01:00:23.304 --> 01:00:25.471
Real zombies are based
on this shit in Haiti.

01:00:25.638 --> 01:00:26.763
It's dead bodies...

01:00:27.638 --> 01:00:30.263
that they turn
into slaves with magic.

01:00:32.013 --> 01:00:33.572
I can't believe you didn't know
that, and you wanna be a vet?

01:00:33.596 --> 01:00:35.471
Is that really what you think
is going on here,

01:00:35.638 --> 01:00:38.846
- Haitian magic?
- This thing is spreading.

01:00:39.471 --> 01:00:42.138
- It wants to spread.
- [Naomi sighs]

01:00:42.304 --> 01:00:44.346
A rat king, uh,
an exploding deer...

01:00:44.513 --> 01:00:45.971
- [banging]
- [Mike screams]

01:00:46.138 --> 01:00:48.096
a dude that wants
to throw up in your mouth!

01:00:48.263 --> 01:00:50.655
It may be down here, but it's
trying like hell to get out there

01:00:50.679 --> 01:00:52.013
into the real world,

01:00:52.763 --> 01:00:54.013
and we gotta try to stop it.

01:00:54.179 --> 01:00:56.554
- [banging]
- [Mike yells]

01:00:57.054 --> 01:00:59.014
- No, thank you.
- You don't wanna save the world?

01:00:59.096 --> 01:01:01.304
[sighs]
I just wanna get home to my kid.

01:01:02.013 --> 01:01:03.888
Okay? If no one else comes

01:01:04.054 --> 01:01:06.888
and we stay in here,
then... we're fine.

01:01:07.054 --> 01:01:08.346
You know? We're contained.

01:01:08.513 --> 01:01:09.929
[engines distantly rumbling]

01:01:10.096 --> 01:01:12.138
[wheezing]

01:01:14.721 --> 01:01:15.804
They're here.

01:01:16.638 --> 01:01:18.054
Oh, fuck yes!

01:01:19.013 --> 01:01:20.054
No, too soon.

01:01:20.763 --> 01:01:23.013
[engines rumbling]

01:01:26.804 --> 01:01:27.888
Oh, shit.

01:01:28.054 --> 01:01:29.929
[light suspenseful tone]

01:01:30.096 --> 01:01:30.929
[whispers] Griffin.

01:01:31.054 --> 01:01:33.221
[engines revving]

01:01:33.388 --> 01:01:35.846
[heavy metal music]

01:01:45.804 --> 01:01:49.346
- [crickets chirping]
- Okay. The Rev,

01:01:49.513 --> 01:01:52.221
- Ironhead, everybody knows, Cuba, Garbage...
- [Cuba] Yeah.

01:01:52.888 --> 01:01:54.804
- And Dr. Steven Friedman.
- Hi.

01:01:54.971 --> 01:01:57.221
[Rev] This better
be worth it, Griffin.

01:01:57.388 --> 01:02:00.304
For a brand-new,
70-inch 4K Ultra

01:02:00.471 --> 01:02:02.179
with a curved screen, asshole?

01:02:02.346 --> 01:02:04.263
Who gives a shit
about a curved screen?

01:02:04.429 --> 01:02:05.971
[lronhead]
if they're such hot titty,

01:02:06.138 --> 01:02:08.638
how come it took you six months
to sell 'em?

01:02:10.346 --> 01:02:12.138
I think a curved screen
sounds cool.

01:02:12.304 --> 01:02:13.804
[lronhead]
Whoa, Griffin.

01:02:13.971 --> 01:02:15.638
- Your place is a mess.
- [Griffin] Uh?

01:02:16.429 --> 01:02:17.804
[doorbell jingle]

01:02:17.971 --> 01:02:20.013
[suspenseful music]

01:02:21.096 --> 01:02:22.554
Whoa, fuck.

01:02:22.721 --> 01:02:24.679
- [lronhead groans]
- [Cuba] God, that is nasty.

01:02:25.679 --> 01:02:27.346
[gagging and coughing]

01:02:29.263 --> 01:02:30.721
[lronhead]
What is that shit?

01:02:33.846 --> 01:02:36.638
Looks like you have
personnel problems, Darryl.

01:02:40.138 --> 01:02:41.971
- [Griffin whimpers]
- [mic feedback]

01:02:42.138 --> 01:02:43.763
[Griffin]
<i>What did you do to my lobby?</i>

01:02:43.929 --> 01:02:46.721
<i>- And where the hell are you?</i>
- Shit, they're inside.

01:02:47.221 --> 01:02:50.763
I'm gonna kill you, shithead.
I'm gonna kill ya.

01:02:51.304 --> 01:02:53.971
<i>- And obviously, you're fired.</i>
- Okay, he saw the wall.

01:02:54.888 --> 01:02:56.471
Jesus, look at that.

01:02:57.429 --> 01:03:00.638
- This shit is insane. It's some kind of joke.
- [elevator voice] <i>Going down.</i>

01:03:00.804 --> 01:03:03.596
Hey, man, you wanna load
eight TVs in the back of my truck,

01:03:03.763 --> 01:03:05.138
you got 20 minutes,

01:03:05.304 --> 01:03:06.697
then I'm getting
the hell out of here

01:03:06.721 --> 01:03:08.138
before the storm comes.

01:03:08.596 --> 01:03:10.796
- [elevator voice] <i>Sub-level one.</i>
- [indistinct chatter]

01:03:11.096 --> 01:03:14.054
I... I had a hygienist,
she was stealing from me.

01:03:14.221 --> 01:03:16.197
- [Cuba] Uh-huh.
- [Steven] I mean, what can you do?

01:03:16.221 --> 01:03:18.179
Personnel problems
are the worst.

01:03:20.138 --> 01:03:21.346
[Cuba]
Hello?

01:03:21.513 --> 01:03:23.763
[Mike heavily breathing]

01:03:25.846 --> 01:03:27.804
[rattling]

01:03:28.304 --> 01:03:31.013
[Griffin] Feast your eyes,
guys. It's your lucky day.

01:03:32.429 --> 01:03:33.679
[chuckles]

01:03:33.846 --> 01:03:35.763
[Trini]
This is the place. [grunts]

01:03:35.929 --> 01:03:37.971
- [crickets chirping]
- [dogs distantly barking]

01:03:40.179 --> 01:03:42.263
- [Robert grunts]
- [grunting]

01:03:44.388 --> 01:03:46.828
[Robert] This is the best storage
plan you could come up with?

01:03:49.638 --> 01:03:51.596
-[groans] -[Trini] Your
back is a time bomb!

01:03:51.763 --> 01:03:53.596
[Robert] Oh, leave me
alone. My back's fine.

01:03:54.721 --> 01:03:56.846
Don't touch the Pontiac.
It's his baby.

01:03:57.013 --> 01:03:59.054
[suspenseful music]

01:04:02.263 --> 01:04:03.929
[soft clicking]

01:04:04.554 --> 01:04:05.554
[lock clicks]

01:04:18.513 --> 01:04:20.679
[soft creaking]

01:04:21.721 --> 01:04:24.013
Oh, boy. Looks old.

01:04:25.221 --> 01:04:27.179
So are we, and we still work.

01:04:27.346 --> 01:04:29.638
[sighs and grunts]

01:04:31.888 --> 01:04:33.197
- [Trini softly] Here.
- I got it.

01:04:33.221 --> 01:04:34.221
[grunting]

01:04:36.013 --> 01:04:38.763
- [Robert grunts]
- [panting]

01:04:40.471 --> 01:04:42.221
[whispers]
Bend your knees, you moron!

01:04:43.638 --> 01:04:46.263
- [groaning] Yo...
- That's it.

01:04:47.471 --> 01:04:48.513
- Okay?
- Oof...

01:04:49.429 --> 01:04:52.596
The shit we get ourselves into,
huh? [chuckles]

01:04:53.554 --> 01:04:54.846
[Robert grunts]

01:04:55.888 --> 01:04:57.054
[click]

01:04:58.179 --> 01:04:59.179
[gun cocks]

01:05:03.471 --> 01:05:06.429
- [whispers] Mom? Really?
- [whispers] Hey, sweetie!

01:05:07.888 --> 01:05:09.138
You look a little heavy.

01:05:10.054 --> 01:05:11.471
What are you doing?

01:05:11.638 --> 01:05:12.721
Just grabbing...

01:05:13.554 --> 01:05:16.971
something...
Out of your hair in two seconds.

01:05:17.513 --> 01:05:19.679
Anthony,
this is my friend, Robert.

01:05:20.221 --> 01:05:23.096
How ya doing, Anthony?
Heard a lot about you.

01:05:25.971 --> 01:05:28.096
If she saw you here,
Janet would kill you.

01:05:28.263 --> 01:05:30.346
- And me.
- Thanksgiving?

01:05:31.096 --> 01:05:32.096
I'll work on it.

01:05:33.096 --> 01:05:33.929
Love you.

01:05:34.096 --> 01:05:35.138
Love you too, Mom.

01:05:37.096 --> 01:05:41.429
So, when you stored this
particular piece of ordinance here...

01:05:42.513 --> 01:05:44.138
- you didn't think...
- What?

01:05:45.263 --> 01:05:48.554
- Your grandkids.
- Oh, come on. It's not like they'd know how to activate it.

01:05:48.721 --> 01:05:50.179
Jesus, you're overcautious.

01:05:51.846 --> 01:05:52.888
Here.

01:05:53.513 --> 01:05:55.433
Take the 72 North.
You'll be there in 20 minutes.

01:05:55.554 --> 01:05:58.554
- I'll get an Uber.
- Sure you don't wanna come? Old times' sake.

01:05:58.721 --> 01:06:00.804
I'd hack up a lung
and get us both killed.

01:06:02.138 --> 01:06:04.179
- [gentle music]
- [softly] Yeah.

01:06:05.304 --> 01:06:09.304
You know, I never stopped having nightmares
about that poor woman in Australia.

01:06:10.596 --> 01:06:12.013
No, me neither.

01:06:14.638 --> 01:06:16.513
You'll try to save
these two, won't you?

01:06:16.971 --> 01:06:18.554
I'll try like hell
to save us all.

01:06:18.721 --> 01:06:20.763
[dramatic tone]

01:06:21.929 --> 01:06:23.429
[rattling]

01:06:23.596 --> 01:06:25.638
[panting]

01:06:27.971 --> 01:06:29.388
[rattling]

01:06:29.554 --> 01:06:30.763
He's not out there.

01:06:30.929 --> 01:06:32.409
I don't care.
I'm not going out there.

01:06:32.971 --> 01:06:34.888
What do you mean?
Those people are gonna die.

01:06:35.388 --> 01:06:37.596
I have Sarah at home,
and Griffin?

01:06:37.763 --> 01:06:39.929
He is a pig. I'm not doing it.

01:06:40.096 --> 01:06:42.596
The guy on the phone said that
he will be here in 20 minutes.

01:06:42.763 --> 01:06:44.763
- Twenty minutes!
- Yeah? Who is that exactly?

01:06:45.263 --> 01:06:48.429
Some guy who talks a big game? Some
lady at Fort Belvoir who has to hang up

01:06:48.596 --> 01:06:51.096
and call back on her own phone?
These people are amateurs, man.

01:06:51.263 --> 01:06:52.804
They're just as scared
as we are.

01:06:52.971 --> 01:06:54.929
Now, if you'd told me
you talked to General...

01:06:55.554 --> 01:06:57.096
Dick Steel or whoever

01:06:57.263 --> 01:06:59.513
and he said half a dozen
Sikorskys were flying in here

01:06:59.679 --> 01:07:02.280
armed with missiles, playing "(Don't
Fear) The Reaper" on big speakers,

01:07:02.304 --> 01:07:04.846
I'd said, "For sure, let's just
kick back and let that happen."

01:07:05.304 --> 01:07:07.721
But they aren't, Naomi, okay?

01:07:08.304 --> 01:07:09.346
They aren't coming.

01:07:10.513 --> 01:07:13.013
Please, please, please!
Do not open that door.

01:07:15.554 --> 01:07:16.721
I got one job.

01:07:17.554 --> 01:07:20.513
All right? It's a shit job,
but it's my shit job.

01:07:20.679 --> 01:07:23.479
This place hired me right out of
prison, and nobody else would do that.

01:07:23.513 --> 01:07:25.929
So, I would very much like
to just once...

01:07:27.096 --> 01:07:28.638
not screw something up.

01:07:31.846 --> 01:07:34.607
You can wait here if you want, but
I'm gonna go stop this zombie shit.

01:07:34.763 --> 01:07:36.888
Y... you... [deeply breathes]

01:07:37.054 --> 01:07:40.554
you are... a lot more
interesting than you look at first.

01:07:42.346 --> 01:07:44.263
Work on that compliment.
Try it again later.

01:07:45.138 --> 01:07:47.346
[rattling]

01:07:47.513 --> 01:07:48.638
Lock the door after me.

01:07:49.596 --> 01:07:51.096
I said rip a hole in the wall.

01:07:52.221 --> 01:07:53.429
You ripped a hole in the wall.

01:07:54.513 --> 01:07:57.138
You were all in. Now I'm all in.

01:07:59.888 --> 01:08:01.096
You coming or what?

01:08:01.846 --> 01:08:03.888
[whimsical, tense music]

01:08:04.929 --> 01:08:06.638
[rattling]

01:08:12.929 --> 01:08:15.072
- That's great work!
- [Garbage] When are you gonna grab one,

01:08:15.096 --> 01:08:18.096
- you lazy piece of shit?
- [Mike heavily breathing]

01:08:19.763 --> 01:08:22.804
- [elevator voice] <i>Going up.</i>
- [playing harmonica]

01:08:25.596 --> 01:08:27.489
- [Naomi] Where's that coming from?
- [Teacake] I dunno.

01:08:27.513 --> 01:08:29.471
[suspenseful tone]

01:08:29.638 --> 01:08:30.798
[whispering] Oh! There he is!

01:08:31.513 --> 01:08:33.554
[ominous music]

01:08:35.138 --> 01:08:36.304
Oh, my God!

01:08:36.471 --> 01:08:37.763
[elevator voice]
<i>Sub-level one.</i>

01:08:42.054 --> 01:08:44.304
[heavily breathing]

01:08:46.763 --> 01:08:49.554
-[Garbage] Oh, my God. What's
wrong with him? [gasps] -[Mike burps]

01:08:49.721 --> 01:08:51.054
[Cuba]
He's got COVID.

01:08:51.221 --> 01:08:53.929
- Yo! Get out of there!
- What do you want?

01:08:54.096 --> 01:08:56.429
- [coughs]
- Hey! Get outta there!

01:08:56.596 --> 01:08:58.697
- [Naomi] Seriously, you should listen to us!
- [Teacake] Get out of there!

01:08:58.721 --> 01:09:00.971
- [retching]
- [splashing]

01:09:02.846 --> 01:09:04.179
[screaming]

01:09:06.221 --> 01:09:08.013
[screaming continues]

01:09:10.013 --> 01:09:11.346
[whimpers and burps]

01:09:12.138 --> 01:09:13.763
Jesus Christ!

01:09:13.929 --> 01:09:16.554
- [rattling]
- [yelling]

01:09:16.721 --> 01:09:18.888
- [banging]
- [Garbage] Open the door!

01:09:19.971 --> 01:09:22.888
- [Mike growls] Naomi!
- [laughs]

01:09:23.054 --> 01:09:25.304
- Mike... hey...
- [yelling]

01:09:28.138 --> 01:09:29.596
- [gunshot]
- [splattering]

01:09:29.763 --> 01:09:31.221
- [Mike groans]
- [clinking]

01:09:31.388 --> 01:09:32.388
[loudly exhales]

01:09:32.429 --> 01:09:34.471
[panting]

01:09:35.013 --> 01:09:37.429
- Mrs. Rooney?
- [panting]

01:09:38.013 --> 01:09:39.471
- [groans]
- [explosion]

01:09:39.638 --> 01:09:41.554
- [splattering]
- [Naomi groaning]

01:09:46.888 --> 01:09:50.513
Something wasn't right
about that young man.

01:09:50.679 --> 01:09:52.721
[suspenseful music]

01:09:56.263 --> 01:09:58.346
[softly]
What in God's name is going on?

01:09:59.679 --> 01:10:00.721
Active shooter.

01:10:03.221 --> 01:10:04.638
- [gun cocks]
- Come on.

01:10:04.804 --> 01:10:06.846
[high-pitched ringing]

01:10:09.263 --> 01:10:10.888
[squelching]

01:10:11.054 --> 01:10:12.804
I gotta get out of here.

01:10:12.971 --> 01:10:14.697
Oh, no. No, no, no, no, no!
No, no, it's cool.

01:10:14.721 --> 01:10:17.596
Uh, it's cool, it's fine.
You had to. Uh, he was, like,

01:10:17.763 --> 01:10:20.054
you know, infected with this
kind of horrible zombie shit

01:10:20.221 --> 01:10:22.364
and he was gonna barf all
over us, into our mouths and...

01:10:22.388 --> 01:10:24.364
- [Griffin] Yeah, I got a gun, shithead!
- Uh, yeah,

01:10:24.388 --> 01:10:26.780
let's get you outta here. Uh,
we're not gonna take the elevator.

01:10:26.804 --> 01:10:28.155
Let's take you over this way.
Come on.

01:10:28.179 --> 01:10:29.299
What do you mean, they left?

01:10:29.429 --> 01:10:30.971
I mean, they're not in the unit.

01:10:31.138 --> 01:10:32.822
<i>- Why the hell not?</i>
- She said there were others

01:10:32.846 --> 01:10:34.888
inside the facility,
and they had to warn them.

01:10:35.054 --> 01:10:36.721
Shit. How many others?

01:10:36.888 --> 01:10:38.263
She didn't say.
She hung up on me.

01:10:38.429 --> 01:10:40.388
I called back four times.
She doesn't answer.

01:10:40.554 --> 01:10:42.471
- When was this?
<i>- Four minutes ago.</i>

01:10:43.179 --> 01:10:45.471
<i>- Changes?</i>
- Only everything.

01:10:45.638 --> 01:10:47.679
[tense music]

01:10:52.346 --> 01:10:54.721
Abigail, there's a storm
on the way.

01:10:54.888 --> 01:10:57.971
<i>If that fungus contacts water,
it'll spread like wildfire.</i>

01:10:58.138 --> 01:10:59.513
We need <i>an aerial view.</i>

01:10:59.679 --> 01:11:01.971
You want satellite
reconnaissance?

01:11:02.138 --> 01:11:04.929
I'll settle for a keyhole. A
ten-minute redirect would do it.

01:11:05.096 --> 01:11:07.763
You're crazy.
Operationally, I mean.

01:11:07.929 --> 01:11:10.929
No, I'm ambitious,
Abigail, and so are you.

01:11:11.096 --> 01:11:12.638
Come on, who do you know?

01:11:12.804 --> 01:11:15.804
- I have a friend at the ADF East.
- There <i>you go!</i>

01:11:15.971 --> 01:11:19.596
I'll be there in eight minutes.
Get eyes overhead ASAP.

01:11:19.763 --> 01:11:21.721
<i>Anyone contaminated
will read hot,</i>

01:11:21.888 --> 01:11:23.888
<i>so look for abnormal
heat signatures.</i>

01:11:24.388 --> 01:11:26.346
Any infected people
leave that place,

01:11:26.513 --> 01:11:29.054
I need to know how many
and where they go.

01:11:29.221 --> 01:11:32.929
- I'm on it.
- Abigail. You know what I have to do, right?

01:11:34.263 --> 01:11:35.388
I read the white paper.

01:11:36.138 --> 01:11:37.221
And you're okay with it?

01:11:38.638 --> 01:11:39.638
Is there a choice?

01:11:40.929 --> 01:11:41.929
No.

01:11:42.679 --> 01:11:44.054
Call you back in six.

01:11:44.221 --> 01:11:45.822
<i>Mrs.</i> Rooney,
you're gonna go up the stairs,

01:11:45.846 --> 01:11:47.554
take two rights
out the side door,

01:11:47.721 --> 01:11:49.405
and that's it, you're good
to go. All right.

01:11:49.429 --> 01:11:51.138
Okay. Oh, Mrs. Rooney!
<i>Mrs.</i> Rooney!

01:11:51.304 --> 01:11:53.554
- [shakily] What?
- The gun! Toss the gun in the river.

01:11:55.096 --> 01:11:56.429
[grunts and stutters]

01:11:56.596 --> 01:11:58.638
[suspenseful music]

01:11:59.179 --> 01:12:00.179
Okay.

01:12:01.263 --> 01:12:03.638
[softly] Jesus Christ. [sighs]

01:12:04.721 --> 01:12:06.554
[Griffin] Hey, I'm armed,
you son of a bitch!

01:12:06.721 --> 01:12:07.929
You hear me?

01:12:08.096 --> 01:12:09.096
[Teacake]
Griffin!

01:12:09.513 --> 01:12:11.346
Yeah, I'm coming in strapped.

01:12:11.513 --> 01:12:13.054
It's Teacake, man! Chill out!

01:12:13.221 --> 01:12:15.221
[crickets chirping]

01:12:15.929 --> 01:12:16.929
You know what?

01:12:19.096 --> 01:12:20.554
I've had it with these clowns.

01:12:23.888 --> 01:12:26.304
- [engine starts]
- [tires screeching]

01:12:26.471 --> 01:12:28.263
[squelching]

01:12:29.888 --> 01:12:31.304
[Griffin]
What the fuck is that?

01:12:33.138 --> 01:12:35.554
Yo! Yo! Griffin!
Put the gun away, you idiot!

01:12:36.054 --> 01:12:38.096
- Hands in the air.
- It's me.

01:12:38.263 --> 01:12:40.096
<i>- My</i> hands are in the air.
- Drop the gun.

01:12:40.263 --> 01:12:42.471
- I don't have a gun, man.
- It... it's true, Darryl,

01:12:42.638 --> 01:12:44.221
he does not appear
to have a gun.

01:12:44.388 --> 01:12:46.513
- You! Glasses! Yeah.
- Oh. Me?

01:12:46.679 --> 01:12:48.179
Get away from that shit, man!

01:12:48.346 --> 01:12:49.666
- Don't touch that!
- [squelching]

01:12:49.763 --> 01:12:51.596
That is some
dangerous shit, okay?

01:12:51.763 --> 01:12:53.429
Down on the floor,
up against the wall!

01:12:54.221 --> 01:12:56.179
Which one, man?
On the floor or the wall?

01:12:56.346 --> 01:12:58.221
[banging]

01:12:58.388 --> 01:13:00.471
- Ironhead?
- [growling]

01:13:00.638 --> 01:13:02.054
[lronhead]
Open this door!

01:13:02.221 --> 01:13:03.614
Ironhead, what the hell
are you doing, man?

01:13:03.638 --> 01:13:05.221
- [banging]
- [lronhead yelling]

01:13:05.388 --> 01:13:07.929
- What'd you lock him in there for?
- Infected.

01:13:08.513 --> 01:13:09.822
- With what?
- [lronhead] Open the door!

01:13:09.846 --> 01:13:11.429
- [Garbage] Open the door!
- Bad shit!

01:13:12.096 --> 01:13:13.346
Open that door.

01:13:13.513 --> 01:13:15.013
- [banging]
- No.

01:13:15.179 --> 01:13:16.322
I'm telling you,
I need to t... [shouts]

01:13:16.346 --> 01:13:17.429
- [gunshot]
- [groans]

01:13:17.596 --> 01:13:19.429
- [clinking]
- [gasps]

01:13:21.054 --> 01:13:24.471
- [softly] You fucking shot me.
- Yeah! An... and I'll shoot you again!

01:13:24.638 --> 01:13:26.888
Unless you open
that goddamn door.

01:13:27.054 --> 01:13:29.054
- [banging]
- Do it!

01:13:29.804 --> 01:13:32.263
- [growling]
- [lronhead] Let me out!

01:13:33.221 --> 01:13:35.513
I will put a goddamn bullet
in your head

01:13:36.346 --> 01:13:38.596
- if you don't open that door.
- [sighing] Fu...

01:13:39.346 --> 01:13:41.221
- [lronhead] Let us out!
- [banging]

01:13:42.596 --> 01:13:43.679
[Griffin]
Keep coming.

01:13:44.263 --> 01:13:45.763
It's a bad idea, man.

01:13:45.929 --> 01:13:47.471
[shakily breathing]

01:13:47.638 --> 01:13:49.888
Darryl? Darryl,
you gotta put the gun down.

01:13:50.054 --> 01:13:52.364
- Darryl... Jeez... [groans]
- [Griffin] Shut up, you nerd!

01:13:52.388 --> 01:13:53.388
Do it.

01:13:53.429 --> 01:13:55.471
[light ominous music]

01:13:58.596 --> 01:13:59.971
- [growling]
- [banging]

01:14:00.138 --> 01:14:01.804
[indistinct shouting]

01:14:04.054 --> 01:14:05.263
[Griffin]
Last chance.

01:14:05.429 --> 01:14:06.804
[clinking]

01:14:08.346 --> 01:14:09.888
- You stupid motherf...
- [Naomi] Hey!

01:14:10.054 --> 01:14:12.804
- [hissing]
- [shouting]

01:14:13.429 --> 01:14:15.013
[Steven]
Give me the gun, Darryl!

01:14:15.179 --> 01:14:16.596
- What are you...
- [gunshots]

01:14:16.763 --> 01:14:18.596
- [grunting]
- [Griffin grunting] Oh, God!

01:14:18.763 --> 01:14:21.471
- [panting] Come on!
- Oh! Quick!

01:14:21.638 --> 01:14:24.114
- Why are you bleeding?
- I'm okay, come on! Come, come, come... look back...

01:14:24.138 --> 01:14:25.596
- [grunting]
- [groans]

01:14:27.013 --> 01:14:28.638
What the hell
are you doing, man?

01:14:28.804 --> 01:14:31.179
Such an asshole.
[indistinct grumbling]

01:14:31.346 --> 01:14:33.346
[dramatic music]

01:14:33.513 --> 01:14:35.679
[panting]

01:14:35.846 --> 01:14:38.596
[groans and grunts]

01:14:41.054 --> 01:14:42.572
- I've never seen anything like that.
- [pants]

01:14:42.596 --> 01:14:43.929
That took a twist, bro!

01:14:44.096 --> 01:14:45.376
You ever seen
anything like that?

01:14:45.429 --> 01:14:46.905
- No! No one has!
- [thunder rumbling]

01:14:46.929 --> 01:14:48.388
That's crazy. This way, come on.

01:14:49.263 --> 01:14:51.346
- [Robert] Stop!
- [groans]

01:14:52.721 --> 01:14:54.554
- [Robert] Abigail, heat sigs.
- Normal.

01:14:55.054 --> 01:14:56.096
Normal!

01:14:56.263 --> 01:14:58.263
- Robert?
- You're Naomi?

01:14:58.429 --> 01:14:59.763
- [panting] Yeah.
- Yo...

01:15:00.888 --> 01:15:03.888
I've had about enough people
pointing guns at me for one night, okay?

01:15:04.054 --> 01:15:07.294
- And you must be Travis.
- [Teacake panting] Yeah. Where's the rest of your crew?

01:15:07.888 --> 01:15:09.263
- I'm it.
- [Naomi] You're it?

01:15:09.429 --> 01:15:11.804
- You're the only person?
- Why is she shouting?

01:15:11.971 --> 01:15:14.114
Gunshot next to the ear, she
can't hear on the right side.

01:15:14.138 --> 01:15:16.179
Ah. Who else has a gun in there?

01:15:16.346 --> 01:15:18.721
So far, everybody but us.

01:15:19.263 --> 01:15:20.638
We'll fix that, come on.

01:15:20.804 --> 01:15:22.721
[panting]

01:15:22.888 --> 01:15:25.013
Ironhead, the door's locked
and you got my key.

01:15:26.013 --> 01:15:28.471
- [rattling]
- [clinking]

01:15:28.638 --> 01:15:30.888
[ominous tone]

01:15:31.054 --> 01:15:32.638
[tense music]

01:15:32.804 --> 01:15:34.054
[Naomi]
I've never shot a gun.

01:15:34.221 --> 01:15:35.554
Fifteen-round magazine.

01:15:37.054 --> 01:15:38.679
Now there's a round
in the chamber.

01:15:38.846 --> 01:15:41.263
Trigger safety right on it.
Nothing to it.

01:15:41.804 --> 01:15:45.179
Okay, you two may have started
the night minimum-wage guards

01:15:45.346 --> 01:15:46.429
working the graveyard,

01:15:47.804 --> 01:15:49.471
but you're
a Green Light Team now.

01:15:50.554 --> 01:15:51.554
Okay?

01:15:51.596 --> 01:15:53.638
[crickets chirping]

01:15:54.888 --> 01:15:56.763
- [grunting]
- What are those?

01:15:57.513 --> 01:15:59.221
Level-four hazmat suits,

01:15:59.388 --> 01:16:02.429
positive pressurization,
self-contained breathing,

01:16:02.596 --> 01:16:05.304
fully chem resistant,
and a two-way radio.

01:16:05.471 --> 01:16:06.471
Put 'em on.

01:16:07.554 --> 01:16:09.846
You have to go back downstairs

01:16:10.013 --> 01:16:11.888
to place this device.

01:16:13.096 --> 01:16:15.471
- It has a select able yield.
- [beeping]

01:16:15.638 --> 01:16:19.054
Point three, five, ten,
or 80 kilotons.

01:16:19.221 --> 01:16:22.804
We'll go with three. Nah,
maybe five, what the hell?

01:16:22.971 --> 01:16:26.263
-Wait a second. Uh, you brought
a nuke? Uh... -[rattling and whirring]

01:16:27.096 --> 01:16:29.471
A nuke? A... a fu...
A fucking suitcase bomb?

01:16:31.388 --> 01:16:33.804
Listen to me.
It is not a suitcase bomb.

01:16:33.971 --> 01:16:36.304
There's no such thing
as a suitcase bomb.

01:16:36.763 --> 01:16:39.388
What kind of invading
ground force carries suitcases?

01:16:39.554 --> 01:16:42.013
That is a nuke. Yo...
Are... what are you, nuts?

01:16:42.179 --> 01:16:44.013
Have you seen
what the fungus can do?

01:16:44.179 --> 01:16:46.179
You're gonna kill everybody
in eastern Kansas, man!

01:16:46.221 --> 01:16:47.721
[Robert]
We're not killing anyone.

01:16:47.888 --> 01:16:50.721
Detonation will be hundreds
of feet underground.

01:16:50.888 --> 01:16:53.388
This immediate area
will be irradiated,

01:16:53.554 --> 01:16:56.054
but there will be
no atmospheric fallout...

01:16:56.888 --> 01:16:58.471
and the problem will be solved.

01:16:59.263 --> 01:17:01.679
Do it right
and we'll all get medals.

01:17:01.846 --> 01:17:02.846
[Naomi]
He's right.

01:17:03.263 --> 01:17:05.304
You saw how fast
that thing spreads.

01:17:05.929 --> 01:17:08.929
You'll carry this down
to sub-level four

01:17:09.096 --> 01:17:11.096
and activate
the triggering mechanism.

01:17:11.263 --> 01:17:12.304
I'll show you how.

01:17:12.888 --> 01:17:14.054
Once it starts,

01:17:14.221 --> 01:17:17.138
you have between
nine and 16 minutes

01:17:17.304 --> 01:17:19.138
to get out
and get a mile away from here.

01:17:19.304 --> 01:17:21.263
Between nine and 16?

01:17:21.429 --> 01:17:24.513
The timer duration's a little
unstable without a metal wire.

01:17:25.179 --> 01:17:28.513
- Okay, yeah. What are you gonna do?
- I'm gonna stay up here,

01:17:28.679 --> 01:17:32.471
and remove any infected
organisms that try to escape the area.

01:17:32.638 --> 01:17:35.596
- Remove?
- I'm going to kill them, Naomi.

01:17:36.096 --> 01:17:37.596
I'm going to execute people

01:17:37.763 --> 01:17:39.929
whose only crime
is that they were exposed

01:17:40.096 --> 01:17:41.304
to a deadly fungus.

01:17:42.221 --> 01:17:43.971
You want my part of the job
or yours?

01:17:44.138 --> 01:17:46.179
[thunder rumbling]

01:17:48.263 --> 01:17:49.383
Yeah, strap that shit on me.

01:17:49.513 --> 01:17:51.554
[dramatic music]

01:17:56.388 --> 01:17:59.054
- [rattling]
- [grunting]

01:17:59.679 --> 01:18:01.013
- Oh...
- [growling]

01:18:02.721 --> 01:18:04.221
[shakily breathing]

01:18:04.388 --> 01:18:05.929
[muffled gagging]

01:18:07.471 --> 01:18:09.596
- [gasping and groaning]
- [thudding]

01:18:09.763 --> 01:18:11.804
[whimpering]

01:18:14.304 --> 01:18:16.346
[loudly whimpering]

01:18:23.763 --> 01:18:25.822
- [Steven] Oh, God! [whimpering]
- [shakily breathing]

01:18:25.846 --> 01:18:27.888
[ominous music]

01:18:28.888 --> 01:18:30.554
Get away from me.
Get away, get back.

01:18:30.721 --> 01:18:32.346
[Garbage]
Easy, man.

01:18:33.179 --> 01:18:34.179
That was...

01:18:35.346 --> 01:18:36.429
horrible.

01:18:36.929 --> 01:18:40.554
So, I think we should all
just get out of here.

01:18:40.721 --> 01:18:43.096
No shit, we're leaving.
You first. Go on.

01:18:43.846 --> 01:18:46.179
- [soft growling]
- [Cuba groaning]

01:18:47.429 --> 01:18:48.429
Cuba?

01:18:49.929 --> 01:18:51.971
[wheezing]

01:18:54.638 --> 01:18:55.721
Cuba?

01:18:58.138 --> 01:19:00.096
- I don't feel so good...
- [explosion]

01:19:00.263 --> 01:19:02.304
[screams and gasps]

01:19:03.096 --> 01:19:04.763
[whimpering]

01:19:05.846 --> 01:19:06.888
I gotta get out of here!

01:19:07.054 --> 01:19:09.054
[dramatic music]

01:19:09.721 --> 01:19:11.763
- [rain splattering]
- [thunder rumbling]

01:19:13.638 --> 01:19:15.888
[loudly breathing]

01:19:16.429 --> 01:19:19.304
[Naomi] <i>Okay, maybe four
minutes</i> to <i>get down there,</i>

01:19:19.471 --> 01:19:21.846
<i>a couple minutes to set it up,
four to get back here.</i>

01:19:22.013 --> 01:19:24.054
[Teacake] <i>No, up is harder.
Six minutes minimum.</i>

01:19:31.679 --> 01:19:33.721
[doorbell jingle]

01:19:42.513 --> 01:19:43.846
[hissing]

01:19:45.263 --> 01:19:46.429
[elevator chimes]

01:19:52.263 --> 01:19:53.596
[elevator voice]
<i>Going down.</i>

01:19:54.763 --> 01:19:56.804
[panting]

01:20:01.429 --> 01:20:02.763
[hissing]

01:20:03.888 --> 01:20:04.888
You've got incoming.

01:20:06.013 --> 01:20:08.471
- Where?
- Around the corner of the building. Ten seconds.

01:20:09.013 --> 01:20:10.388
<i>Male, moving fast,</i>

01:20:10.554 --> 01:20:12.763
<i>major heat signature.
On the left.</i>

01:20:13.846 --> 01:20:15.429
<i>- I got nothing!
- More</i> left!

01:20:16.263 --> 01:20:18.263
- Nothing!
<i>- More</i> left... He's right behind you!

01:20:18.846 --> 01:20:20.513
- [groans]
- [screaming]

01:20:20.679 --> 01:20:22.638
Get this shit off of me!

01:20:22.804 --> 01:20:26.304
- [gunshots]
- [groaning]

01:20:27.471 --> 01:20:30.138
[groans] Son of a bitch!

01:20:31.054 --> 01:20:32.763
[groans]

01:20:32.929 --> 01:20:34.888
- [thudding]
- [groaning]

01:20:35.596 --> 01:20:37.638
[loudly breathing]

01:20:39.054 --> 01:20:40.721
[Teacake]
<i>Damn, this thing's heavy.</i>

01:20:40.888 --> 01:20:42.013
[Naomi]
<i>Want me to carry it?</i>

01:20:43.013 --> 01:20:44.013
[Teacake]
<i>I got it.</i>

01:20:44.138 --> 01:20:46.429
[tense music]

01:20:47.346 --> 01:20:48.429
[grunts]

01:20:49.554 --> 01:20:50.804
[alarm distantly blares]

01:20:50.971 --> 01:20:52.596
[Teacake]
<i>Okay, chuck it down there?</i>

01:20:52.763 --> 01:20:54.530
<i>- Hope for the best?</i>
- [Naomi]I <i>don't think so.</i>

01:20:54.554 --> 01:20:57.638
- [groaning]
- Robert, are you all right?

01:20:57.804 --> 01:20:59.679
<i>It's my fucking back.
I can still</i>

01:20:59.846 --> 01:21:01.526
<i>- take them out from here.</i>
- [softly] Shit.

01:21:08.096 --> 01:21:10.096
[panting]

01:21:10.888 --> 01:21:13.096
[Naomi]
<i>Okay, almost there. Yeah.</i>

01:21:13.263 --> 01:21:14.804
[panting]

01:21:14.971 --> 01:21:17.304
<i>I got it.</i> [grunts]

01:21:20.638 --> 01:21:22.554
[soft squelching]

01:21:22.721 --> 01:21:24.763
[suspenseful music]

01:21:25.263 --> 01:21:27.138
[Ironhead growling]

01:21:27.971 --> 01:21:29.013
[softly] Go on.

01:21:30.304 --> 01:21:32.221
[music increases]

01:21:32.388 --> 01:21:34.429
[rain splattering]

01:21:36.429 --> 01:21:38.471
[grunting and panting]

01:21:40.846 --> 01:21:43.096
[squelching and creaking]

01:21:45.179 --> 01:21:46.721
- [explosion]
- [splattering]

01:21:46.888 --> 01:21:47.929
[grunts]

01:21:49.471 --> 01:21:50.846
[softly] Nobody leaves.

01:21:51.013 --> 01:21:53.054
[gunshots]

01:21:55.429 --> 01:21:57.096
[loud explosion]

01:21:58.263 --> 01:22:00.929
-[Robert groaning] -Robert,
what the hell is happening there?

01:22:01.096 --> 01:22:03.138
[fire whooshing]

01:22:03.596 --> 01:22:04.596
[Griffin]
What was that?

01:22:04.763 --> 01:22:06.596
[ominous music]

01:22:06.763 --> 01:22:07.804
Where are you going?

01:22:09.263 --> 01:22:11.721
- [growling]
- [squelching]

01:22:13.596 --> 01:22:15.572
- [Teacake]How <i>much time</i> we <i>have to get out?</i>
- [Naomi] <i>At least nine minutes</i>

01:22:15.596 --> 01:22:17.471
<i>- after we start the timer.</i>
- [Teacake] <i>Yeah,</i>

01:22:17.638 --> 01:22:19.958
<i>- what if that's not enough?</i>
- [Naomi]I <i>don't know, we die?</i>

01:22:20.304 --> 01:22:22.346
[panting and grunting]

01:22:23.721 --> 01:22:26.221
- [Naomi] <i>It's stuck!</i>
- [Teacake] <i>Hang on, let me help.</i>

01:22:27.221 --> 01:22:29.304
- [grunting]
- [creaking]

01:22:29.763 --> 01:22:30.888
[Naomi]
<i>Watch your step.</i>

01:22:35.346 --> 01:22:37.888
[Teacake]
<i>Oh, you've gotta be kidding me.</i>

01:22:39.013 --> 01:22:41.388
<i>- What happened?</i>
- [Naomi] <i>It found water.</i>

01:22:41.554 --> 01:22:44.638
<i>Uh, if it makes it through that
pipe, it'll get into the groundwater</i>

01:22:44.804 --> 01:22:48.554
<i>- and then that will take it through to the Missouri River.
- Let's blow this shit up.</i>

01:22:48.721 --> 01:22:50.441
<i>Do you think we have</i>
to <i>put it in that room?</i>

01:22:50.513 --> 01:22:52.763
- [dramatic music]
- [squelching]

01:22:55.596 --> 01:22:56.804
<i>Nah, here's fine.</i>

01:23:05.929 --> 01:23:07.638
[clicking]

01:23:08.638 --> 01:23:10.013
[hissing]

01:23:10.179 --> 01:23:11.638
[beeping]

01:23:11.804 --> 01:23:14.013
<i>Yo, wait,
the timer's already going.</i>

01:23:15.346 --> 01:23:18.888
<i>Oh, my God!
That son of a bitch started it!</i>

01:23:19.054 --> 01:23:20.096
Come <i>on!</i>

01:23:25.596 --> 01:23:26.846
<i>I hate this job.</i>

01:23:27.013 --> 01:23:29.054
[panting]

01:23:32.638 --> 01:23:35.763
We're <i>never gonna make it out of
here in these. Take it off! Take it off!</i>

01:23:38.096 --> 01:23:40.013
[squelching]

01:23:40.179 --> 01:23:41.804
[ominous music]

01:23:41.971 --> 01:23:43.346
[grunting]

01:23:46.013 --> 01:23:47.179
Oh, shit.

01:23:48.138 --> 01:23:50.179
[panting]

01:23:50.346 --> 01:23:52.763
- How much time we got?
- The timer duration is unstable.

01:23:52.929 --> 01:23:54.739
- What the hell does that mean?
- It might go off early,

01:23:54.763 --> 01:23:56.721
it might go off late.
Just hurry up!

01:23:57.221 --> 01:23:59.346
[panting and grunting]

01:23:59.513 --> 01:24:01.763
[dramatic music]

01:24:04.263 --> 01:24:07.179
[shakily breathes] Things are
getting a bit unpleasant here, Abigail.

01:24:07.346 --> 01:24:09.679
- [Abigail] Fungus is moving towards you.
<i>- No kidding.</i>

01:24:10.346 --> 01:24:11.763
[panting]

01:24:12.929 --> 01:24:15.179
- Go to the door. Right.
- [growling]

01:24:16.471 --> 01:24:18.013
[groans]

01:24:18.179 --> 01:24:19.971
- [whirring]
- [Griffin] Keep moving!

01:24:23.138 --> 01:24:24.596
[doorbell jingles]

01:24:25.929 --> 01:24:28.304
- [gunshots]
- [Griffin yells and groans]

01:24:28.471 --> 01:24:30.804
[grunts] Fuck...

01:24:30.971 --> 01:24:33.013
- [gunshots]
- [Griffin shouting]

01:24:34.554 --> 01:24:36.554
- [clinking]
- [panting]

01:24:38.763 --> 01:24:41.013
[dramatic music]

01:24:45.179 --> 01:24:47.638
- [beeping]
- [static]

01:24:50.346 --> 01:24:52.388
[panting]

01:24:55.888 --> 01:24:59.054
- Hey, asshole! You're all out!
- [loudly breathing]

01:24:59.221 --> 01:25:00.846
I heard your clip go dry.

01:25:02.221 --> 01:25:05.013
- [Robert] You think so? Come on out here and find out!
- [grunts]

01:25:08.388 --> 01:25:10.388
[snarling]

01:25:10.554 --> 01:25:12.596
[ominous music]

01:25:14.346 --> 01:25:15.638
[grunts and gasps]

01:25:16.346 --> 01:25:18.013
I think I'm fucked up.

01:25:18.179 --> 01:25:20.846
- [whimpers]
- [gunshots]

01:25:21.013 --> 01:25:22.346
- [thudding]
- [splattering]

01:25:22.513 --> 01:25:24.054
[dramatic music]

01:25:24.221 --> 01:25:25.513
[grunts]

01:25:26.138 --> 01:25:28.346
- [whimpering]
- [squelching]

01:25:28.513 --> 01:25:30.096
[Robert]
You're next, you bastard!

01:25:30.679 --> 01:25:32.929
[heavily breathing,
softly groaning]

01:25:38.096 --> 01:25:39.471
You trashed my bike, huh?

01:25:39.638 --> 01:25:41.846
- [gasping]
- Fine, I'll take your ride.

01:25:42.013 --> 01:25:45.054
This is some every-man-for-himself
kind of shit going on here.

01:25:46.138 --> 01:25:47.138
[groans]

01:25:47.763 --> 01:25:50.346
- You gotta go.
- Go fuck yourself.

01:25:51.554 --> 01:25:52.679
[horn honking]

01:25:53.596 --> 01:25:55.179
[engine shuts off]

01:25:57.471 --> 01:25:59.471
[crickets chirping]

01:26:00.804 --> 01:26:02.804
Take your greasy hand
out of his pants.

01:26:04.138 --> 01:26:05.138
[grunts]

01:26:05.638 --> 01:26:06.888
Who the hell are you?

01:26:07.054 --> 01:26:08.888
- Okay to go?
- Okay to go!

01:26:09.054 --> 01:26:10.054
Go where?

01:26:10.554 --> 01:26:12.346
- [gunshots]
- [groans]

01:26:12.513 --> 01:26:14.804
- [clinking]
- [thudding]

01:26:15.388 --> 01:26:17.596
- [groaning]
- [Trini]You were right.

01:26:17.763 --> 01:26:19.554
Your back is fine.

01:26:19.721 --> 01:26:20.721
[Robert]
Oh, shut up.

01:26:20.846 --> 01:26:22.429
[dramatic music]

01:26:22.596 --> 01:26:24.476
[Teacake] Is that guy
trying to kill us or what?

01:26:26.346 --> 01:26:29.054
- Oh!
- Oh, shit. [panting]

01:26:29.513 --> 01:26:31.888
- [Garbage whimpering]
- Yo! You gotta get out of here!

01:26:33.554 --> 01:26:35.221
[squelching]

01:26:36.471 --> 01:26:38.804
-[whimpering] -[Teacake]
Oh, that's not so great.

01:26:38.971 --> 01:26:41.763
-Were you paying attention when
he showed you how to... -[gunshots]

01:26:41.929 --> 01:26:45.013
- [thudding]
- Yeah. You were.

01:26:48.138 --> 01:26:50.804
- [beeping]
- [whirring]

01:26:52.846 --> 01:26:54.888
[squelching]

01:26:55.804 --> 01:26:59.054
- Trini, we need to leave. Now!
- [Teacake] Come on! Come on!

01:26:59.846 --> 01:27:01.646
- No go! No go! No go!
- [indistinct shouting]

01:27:01.721 --> 01:27:04.096
-Okay... -Jeez... We're clean,
we're clean! We're clean!

01:27:04.263 --> 01:27:05.763
[Robert]
We... we have to leave!

01:27:05.929 --> 01:27:07.096
Holy shit, Griffin's dead.

01:27:07.263 --> 01:27:08.721
Yeah, that guy was an asshole.

01:27:08.888 --> 01:27:10.763
- [groaning]
- [grunting]

01:27:11.638 --> 01:27:13.138
You started that timer on us!

01:27:13.304 --> 01:27:15.513
- I knew you could get out.
- [grunts]

01:27:15.679 --> 01:27:17.888
- You did not know that!
- I had a hunch.

01:27:18.346 --> 01:27:20.388
- [shouts] You had a hunch?
- A solid hunch!

01:27:20.554 --> 01:27:22.804
[dramatic music]

01:27:23.263 --> 01:27:25.596
[groaning]

01:27:25.763 --> 01:27:28.804
I did not think these two
shitheads were gonna make it.

01:27:29.596 --> 01:27:31.929
- [Robert] We haven't yet.
- How much time we got?

01:27:32.096 --> 01:27:34.721
[Robert] It should've gone off a
minute and seven seconds ago.

01:27:34.888 --> 01:27:36.614
You brought a defective
suitcase bomb, didn't you?

01:27:36.638 --> 01:27:38.513
There is no such thing
as a suitcase bomb.

01:27:38.679 --> 01:27:40.263
I already told him that.

01:27:40.429 --> 01:27:41.971
The timer duration is unstable.

01:27:42.138 --> 01:27:43.697
[shouting] Would you all
please stop saying that?

01:27:43.721 --> 01:27:45.763
[engine rumbling]

01:27:47.179 --> 01:27:48.179
How about now?

01:27:48.554 --> 01:27:50.388
[beeping]

01:27:50.554 --> 01:27:52.971
[squelching]

01:27:53.138 --> 01:27:54.304
[static]

01:27:54.471 --> 01:27:56.138
- [muffled rumbling]
- [whooshing]

01:27:56.304 --> 01:27:58.679
- [loud explosion]
- [whirring]

01:27:58.846 --> 01:28:00.888
[loud crashing and rumbling]

01:28:05.888 --> 01:28:08.138
- [loud explosion]
- [buzzing and crackling]

01:28:09.263 --> 01:28:11.304
[tires screeching]

01:28:20.429 --> 01:28:21.888
[grunting and yelling]

01:28:31.221 --> 01:28:33.054
Oh, shit, my son's car!

01:28:33.221 --> 01:28:35.263
[loud rumbling]

01:28:40.388 --> 01:28:42.638
[panting]

01:28:45.596 --> 01:28:47.721
[poignant music]

01:28:47.888 --> 01:28:49.929
[panting and sighing]

01:28:51.971 --> 01:28:54.013
[distant siren blaring]

01:28:54.679 --> 01:28:56.888
[woman on PA]
<i>A nuclear event has occurred.</i>

01:28:57.054 --> 01:29:01.304
<i>Ionized radiation detected
in zone five. This is not a drill.</i>

01:29:01.471 --> 01:29:04.239
- [Jerabek] Someone tell me what the hell just happened!
- [shakily breathing]

01:29:04.263 --> 01:29:05.663
[woman on PA]
<i>A nuclear event has</i>...

01:29:05.763 --> 01:29:06.596
[reporter]
<i>I'm sorry, Colonel,</i>

01:29:06.763 --> 01:29:08.346
<i>that's not accurate.</i>

01:29:08.513 --> 01:29:10.572
<i>In the hours immediately
following the Atchison incident,</i>

01:29:10.596 --> 01:29:12.721
<i>you tried to silence
the very people who prevented</i>

01:29:12.888 --> 01:29:15.197
<i>- the spread of the fungus!
- Hold on. Hold on, hold on, now.</i>

01:29:15.221 --> 01:29:17.489
<i>- No, no, but this is...</i>
- [Robert] Yeah, go ahead, jerk off.

01:29:17.513 --> 01:29:19.239
<i>- you tried...</i> [indistinctly
continues] -Try to spin your ass

01:29:19.263 --> 01:29:21.888
- out of this one. [chuckles]
- [cross talk on TV]

01:29:22.054 --> 01:29:24.304
[Jerabek] <i>...preparations</i>
we <i>are now making to ensure</i>

01:29:24.471 --> 01:29:27.697
<i>- that nothing like this happens in the future, do you understa...</i>
- [sighs] Asshole.

01:29:27.721 --> 01:29:29.489
[reporter] <i>And you may
well have been successful</i>

01:29:29.513 --> 01:29:31.804
<i>if not for the heroic actions
of this man,</i>

01:29:31.971 --> 01:29:34.554
<i>- retired DTRA officer Robert Quinn...</i>
- [Robert] Yeah.

01:29:34.721 --> 01:29:36.804
<i>Whose white paper report
from 2009</i>

01:29:36.971 --> 01:29:39.451
<i>- warned of the possibility of this very incident.</i>
- [chuckles]

01:29:39.513 --> 01:29:40.780
[Jerabek]
<i>No, I don't think people...</i>

01:29:40.804 --> 01:29:42.471
[indistinctly continues]

01:29:42.638 --> 01:29:45.513
So, what's the over
on how long till he gets fired?

01:29:45.679 --> 01:29:47.513
- [indistinct chatter on TV]
- 48 hours?

01:29:50.763 --> 01:29:51.763
Abigail?

01:29:53.138 --> 01:29:55.888
- It's Shani, actually.
- [Robert] Shani.

01:29:56.929 --> 01:29:59.596
My white paper got out.
That was you.

01:29:59.763 --> 01:30:03.179
- Mama didn't raise no patsies.
- Nice!

01:30:03.346 --> 01:30:04.971
So are your drugs, apparently.

01:30:07.638 --> 01:30:10.763
Hey! Macallan, how did you know?

01:30:11.846 --> 01:30:13.679
I cheated. It was in your file.

01:30:13.846 --> 01:30:14.846
Yeah?

01:30:15.346 --> 01:30:17.763
I wanted to... thank you.

01:30:18.846 --> 01:30:19.846
For what?

01:30:20.804 --> 01:30:22.679
For reminding me why I joined.

01:30:22.846 --> 01:30:23.929
To blow shit up?

01:30:24.096 --> 01:30:26.054
[gentle music]

01:30:26.221 --> 01:30:27.221
To be there...

01:30:28.221 --> 01:30:29.346
when needed.

01:30:29.513 --> 01:30:30.596
And you were.

01:30:32.054 --> 01:30:33.929
Hey, mission ain't over.

01:30:34.096 --> 01:30:35.513
Pour me a large one.

01:30:35.679 --> 01:30:37.513
[Shani]
Not on the painkillers, dummy.

01:30:37.679 --> 01:30:38.804
[scoffs]

01:30:42.888 --> 01:30:44.804
[children
indistinctly chattering]

01:30:44.971 --> 01:30:47.638
- [birds chirping]
- [Naomi giggling]

01:30:47.804 --> 01:30:50.054
[laughing]

01:30:51.429 --> 01:30:52.929
- [shouts]
- [both] Oh!

01:30:53.096 --> 01:30:54.096
[laughter]

01:30:54.138 --> 01:30:55.471
[Naomi]
Careful!

01:30:55.638 --> 01:30:57.554
- [Teacake] Look out.
- [laughs]

01:30:59.054 --> 01:31:00.054
[grunts]

01:31:04.554 --> 01:31:07.554
[sharply inhales]
I was about, like, uh,

01:31:08.596 --> 01:31:10.429
16, 17, thereabouts.

01:31:10.596 --> 01:31:12.846
Me and my boys were rolling
around, got the munchies,

01:31:13.013 --> 01:31:16.513
and we pull off and we get some
Twinkies or something like that.

01:31:16.679 --> 01:31:18.739
I'm the last one in, though,
so they get the good stuff,

01:31:18.763 --> 01:31:20.346
and all that's left
when I get there

01:31:20.513 --> 01:31:22.513
is this thing called
Aunt Sarah's Teacake.

01:31:22.679 --> 01:31:25.513
-So... -This is where the
nickname came from?

01:31:26.346 --> 01:31:29.846
I buy it. I like it. I say I wanna
go back, get another one,

01:31:30.013 --> 01:31:32.929
and for some reason, my boys
think this is some hilarious shit,

01:31:33.096 --> 01:31:34.929
- I mean, good stuff, so...
- Hmm. Mm.

01:31:35.096 --> 01:31:37.456
-[Sarah laughs] -[chuckles]
they started saying things like,

01:31:37.513 --> 01:31:40.888
- "Hey, Teacake! Where's your teacake, huh?"
- [laughing continues]

01:31:41.888 --> 01:31:45.846
You know? Crazy, brilliant,
witty shi... uh, stuff

01:31:46.346 --> 01:31:47.929
- like that, and that was it.
- Stuff.

01:31:48.096 --> 01:31:50.179
- [Sarah laughing]
- [Teacake] I was Teacake.

01:31:51.054 --> 01:31:53.179
And I never really heard
my given name since.

01:31:54.054 --> 01:31:55.221
Nobody even asked me.

01:31:55.388 --> 01:31:57.304
- [birds chirping]
- [music continues]

01:31:58.179 --> 01:31:59.179
Till you.

01:31:59.263 --> 01:32:01.054
[indistinct chatter]

01:32:01.221 --> 01:32:03.179
[chuckles] See, Travis?

01:32:03.346 --> 01:32:04.513
Loquacious.

01:32:09.429 --> 01:32:10.429
[chuckles]

01:32:14.471 --> 01:32:16.263
- [laughter]
- [Teacake groans and grunts]

01:32:16.429 --> 01:32:18.471
[laughter]

01:32:21.846 --> 01:32:24.096
[birds chirping]

01:32:27.679 --> 01:32:29.346
[bellowing]

01:32:31.554 --> 01:32:32.804
[huffing]

01:32:36.346 --> 01:32:38.013
[grunting]

01:32:40.846 --> 01:32:42.221
[gurgling and retching]

